window.DBD_DATA.perks.push(...[{"id":"wicked","rank":73,"tier":"B","roles":["Anti-Tunnel","Information","Rescue"],"summary":"After any unhook, see the Killer for up to 20 seconds; if your first hook is in the Basement, your self-unhook chance there becomes guaranteed.","metaStatus":"Good","skillLevel":"Low–Medium","soloQ":4,"swf":3,"unlockPriority":"High","glossaryKeys":["aura-reading","hook-state","anti-tunnel","tunneling"],"useCases":["Use the long post-unhook Killer Aura read to route safely and avoid immediate reacquisition.","Guarantee escape from a first-stage Basement hook when the match gives you that rare but dangerous situation.","Pair the Aura read with anti-tunnel perks so you know exactly how the Killer is playing the rescue."],"counters":["The guaranteed self-unhook only applies to first-stage Basement hooks.","Outside Basement, the perk's main value is information rather than direct protection.","A Killer can still tunnel you despite being visible."],"pros":["Twenty seconds of post-unhook Killer Aura is excellent information.","Basement clause can completely erase an otherwise difficult rescue obligation.","Works in Solo Q without coordination."],"cons":["Basement jackpot is inconsistent.","Does not create Endurance or direct distance.","Part of its power may never appear in many Trials."],"analysis":["Wicked earns this position because its consistent half is already useful: a long Killer Aura read after every unhook. Twenty seconds is enough to understand whether the Killer is returning, rotating, proxying, or committing elsewhere, which helps the rescued Survivor make much better pathing decisions.","The Basement clause is the spectacular upside. A guaranteed first-stage self-unhook can free three teammates from having to enter one of the most dangerous rescue locations in the game. It can also completely surprise a Killer who assumes Basement pressure will force a rescue.","The problem is frequency. Many matches never put you on a first-stage Basement hook, so the perk must be judged primarily as post-unhook information rather than a guaranteed Deliverance substitute.","That consistent Aura read keeps Wicked comfortably in upper B. The rare Basement activation can make it look much stronger, but our ranking does not assume the map and hook placement will cooperate."],"verdict":"Excellent post-unhook information with a rare Basement escape jackpot. Wicked is useful every time you are rescued and occasionally game-changing when Basement enters the equation.","publicationStatus":"published","tags":["Self-Unhook"],"queueRatingStatus":"reviewed","rankRange":[65,85],"rankConfidence":"Low","rankStatus":"stable","evidenceStatus":"inherited","acquisition":{"type":"character","sourceCharacter":"Sable Ward"},"synergyPerkIds":["off-the-record","will-to-live","kindred","resurgence"],"synergyOther":[],"antiSynergyPerkIds":[],"archetypeRatings":[],"reviewFlags":["v15-schema-migrated","rank-review-applied","queue-rating:audit-partial-plus-normalized"],"synergies":["Off the Record","Will to Live","Kindred","Resurgence"],"antiSynergies":[],"name":"Wicked","alternateName":null,"source":"Sable Ward","status":"Live 10.2.0","currentEffect":"After you are unhooked by any means, reveals the Killer's Aura to you for 16/18/20 seconds. While hooked in the Basement during the first Hook Stage, your chance to succeed at a Self-Unhook attempt is 100%. It does not apply during the second Hook Stage or when you are the last Survivor standing.","activation":["Be unhooked by any means to reveal the Killer's Aura.","For the Basement effect, be hooked in the Basement during the first Hook Stage and not be the last Survivor standing.","Ends/deactivates when: Killer Aura reveal ends after 16/18/20 seconds.","Ends/deactivates when: The Basement self-unhook effect does not apply in second Hook Stage or when last Survivor standing."],"patchNote":"Latest live balance change (9.3.2): Reverted to the previous version (16/18/20 s Killer Aura after unhook; guaranteed Basement first-stage self-unhook) after the perk was disabled in 9.3.0.","plainEnglishSummary":"After an unhook, shows the Killer's Aura; if hooked in the Basement, it guarantees a first-stage self-unhook attempt can succeed.","cooldown":null,"duration":["Killer Aura reveal after unhook: 16/18/20 seconds."],"tokenOrStackBehavior":null,"oncePerTrialOrOtherLimits":null,"statusEffectsInvolved":[],"specialInteractions":["The Basement self-unhook effect only applies during the first Hook Stage and is excluded when last Survivor standing."],"sourceCharacter":"Sable Ward","isGeneralPerk":false,"currentLivePatchVerified":"10.2.0"},{"id":"boon-exponential","rank":74,"tier":"B","roles":["Boon","Anti-Slug","Recovery"],"summary":"Inside its 24-metre Boon radius, Survivors recover from the Dying State up to twice as fast and can fully self-recover.","metaStatus":"Good","skillLevel":"Medium","soloQ":3,"swf":4,"unlockPriority":"Medium","glossaryKeys":["anti-slug","dying-state"],"useCases":["Protect a high-traffic area from mass slugging.","Create a recovery zone where downed teammates can stand without another Survivor touching them.","Stack anti-slug value with other Boon effects on the same Totem."],"counters":["Only downed Survivors inside the Boon radius receive the effect.","The Killer can snuff the Totem.","If the Killer hooks promptly instead of slugging, the perk may never matter."],"pros":["100% faster recovery is substantial.","Unlocks full self-recovery for every Survivor in the zone.","Can punish multi-Survivor slugging extremely hard."],"cons":["Very situational against Killers who hook normally.","Totem placement determines coverage.","Requires blessing time before the anti-slug insurance exists."],"analysis":["Boon: Exponential ranks this position because its ceiling during a slugging snowball is enormous. Survivors in the zone recover up to 100% faster and can fully stand themselves up, which can make leaving multiple players on the ground strategically impossible for the Killer.","The teamwide nature is the most important distinction from perks like Unbreakable. One Totem can potentially protect several Survivors, and the benefit remains available as long as the Boon survives. On maps where the radius covers several connected tiles, that can alter the Killer's entire downing strategy.","The downside is opportunity frequency. A Killer who immediately hooks each downed Survivor may never give Exponential a meaningful trigger. The user can spend time finding and blessing a Totem only for the match to contain no slugging at all.","That makes it an excellent specialist rather than a general-purpose choice. In Boon builds the opportunity cost is lower because the same Totem also carries Circle of Healing, Shadow Step, or Steadfast, improving the overall investment."],"verdict":"One of the strongest anti-slug zones in the game, but only when slugging actually happens inside it. Excellent Boon-stack value, inconsistent standalone value.","publicationStatus":"published","tags":[],"queueRatingStatus":"reviewed","rankRange":null,"rankConfidence":"Not assessed","rankStatus":"inherited","evidenceStatus":"inherited","acquisition":{"type":"character","sourceCharacter":"Jonah Vasquez"},"synergyPerkIds":["boon-circle-of-healing","boon-shadow-step","conviction","soul-guard"],"synergyOther":[],"antiSynergyPerkIds":[],"archetypeRatings":[],"reviewFlags":["v15-schema-migrated","queue-rating:normalized-tier-plus-v14-specialization-signal"],"synergies":["Boon: Circle of Healing","Boon: Shadow Step","Conviction","Soul Guard"],"antiSynergies":[],"name":"Boon: Exponential","alternateName":null,"source":"Jonah Vasquez","status":"Live 10.2.0","currentEffect":"Bless a Dull or Hex Totem. Survivors within 24 metres recover from the Dying State 90/95/100% faster and can recover themselves fully from the Dying State.","activation":["Bless a Dull or Hex Totem.","Be within 24 metres and in the Dying State for recovery effects.","Ends/deactivates when: Effects end outside Boon range or when the totem is snuffed."],"patchNote":"Latest live balance change (unknown): No material live balance change could be verified from available patch history.","plainEnglishSummary":"A Boon Totem speeds Dying recovery and enables nearby Survivors to pick themselves up.","cooldown":null,"duration":[],"tokenOrStackBehavior":null,"oncePerTrialOrOtherLimits":"One active Boon Totem per Survivor; equipped Boons apply to that totem.","statusEffectsInvolved":[],"specialInteractions":["Unlocks Self-Recovery from the Dying State while in range."],"sourceCharacter":"Jonah Vasquez","isGeneralPerk":false,"currentLivePatchVerified":"10.2.0"},{"id":"bada-bada-boom","rank":75,"tier":"B","roles":["Chase"],"summary":"After 20% generator repair, trap a Window; if the Killer vaults it, they suffer 50% Hindered for 6 seconds.","metaStatus":"Good","skillLevel":"Medium–High","soloQ":3,"swf":4,"unlockPriority":"Medium","glossaryKeys":["looping","pressure"],"useCases":["Trap a powerful Window the Killer is likely to vault during chase.","Create a massive slowdown that lets a Survivor leave the tile after the Killer follows.","Mark the trapped Window for teammates through its yellow Aura."],"counters":["The Killer must vault the trapped Window before the timer expires.","Some Killers can play the tile without ever vaulting.","Requires prior generator repair and a good Window location."],"pros":["50% Hindered for 6 seconds is enormous.","Low 20% repair charge requirement.","Can affect another Survivor's chase, not only your own."],"cons":["Very trigger-dependent.","Trap can expire unused.","Experienced Killers may route around it."],"analysis":["Bada Bada Boom ranks this position because the successful trigger is excellent but hard to force. A Killer vaulting the trapped Window eats a 50% Hindered effect for six seconds, enough to completely break many chase sequences.","The low repair requirement means charging it is not the problem. The real challenge is predicting a Window the Killer will actually vault before the trap expires.","Good map knowledge raises the ceiling because some strong structures naturally encourage Killer vaults. The yellow Aura also lets teammates recognize the trapped resource.","It remains mid-B because many Killers can refuse the interaction. A trap that never fires creates no chase swing regardless of how impressive the number looks."],"verdict":"A brutal Window trap when the Killer cooperates. Bada Bada Boom has huge payoff and unreliable agency, which makes it a specialist rather than a default chase perk.","publicationStatus":"published","tags":["Trap","Hindered"],"queueRatingStatus":"reviewed","rankRange":null,"rankConfidence":"Not assessed","rankStatus":"inherited","evidenceStatus":"inherited","acquisition":{"type":"character","sourceCharacter":"Dustin Henderson"},"synergyPerkIds":["chemical-trap","lithe","windows-of-opportunity","quick-quiet"],"synergyOther":[],"antiSynergyPerkIds":[],"archetypeRatings":[],"reviewFlags":["v15-schema-migrated","queue-rating:normalized-tier-plus-v14-specialization-signal"],"synergies":["Chemical Trap","Lithe","Windows of Opportunity","Quick & Quiet"],"antiSynergies":[],"name":"Bada Bada Boom","alternateName":null,"source":"Dustin Henderson","status":"Live 10.2.0","currentEffect":"After completing 20% worth of Generator repairs, the perk activates. While active, use the Active Ability button next to a Window to install a Trap that remains for up to 40/50/60 seconds. When the Killer vaults through the trapped Window, they suffer 50% Hindered for 6 seconds. The trap ends after triggering or timing out, and all Survivors see the trapped Window's yellow Aura.","activation":["Accumulate 20% total Generator repair progress.","While active, use the Active Ability button next to a Window to install the trap.","Ends/deactivates when: The trap ends when triggered or when its timer expires."],"patchNote":"Latest live balance change (9.4.0): Introduced with a 20% repair threshold and 40/50/60-second trap duration.","plainEnglishSummary":"After enough Generator repair, trap a Window to Hinder the Killer when they vault through it.","cooldown":null,"duration":["Trap duration: 40/50/60 seconds.","Killer Hindered: 6 seconds."],"tokenOrStackBehavior":null,"oncePerTrialOrOtherLimits":"The trap is consumed on trigger; another requires qualifying progress and installation.","statusEffectsInvolved":["Hindered"],"specialInteractions":["The Killer is Hindered when vaulting through the trapped Window.","All Survivors see the trapped Window's yellow Aura."],"sourceCharacter":"Dustin Henderson","isGeneralPerk":false,"currentLivePatchVerified":"10.2.0"},{"id":"fast-track","rank":76,"tier":"B","roles":["Objective","Rescue","Skill Check"],"summary":"Each time you unhook another Survivor, gain one Token up to three; a Great generator Skill Check spends all Tokens for 5% permanent progress each.","metaStatus":"Good","skillLevel":"Medium–High","soloQ":3,"swf":3,"unlockPriority":"Medium","glossaryKeys":["pressure","hook-state"],"useCases":["Turn successful rescue participation into permanent generator progress.","Bank multiple Tokens for a single 10–15% objective swing.","Pair with Skill Check support so the conversion is reliable."],"counters":["You must personally unhook Survivors to earn Tokens.","Requires a Great basic Skill Check to cash out.","Maximum storage is only three Tokens."],"pros":["Permanent generator progress is powerful.","Rescue activity naturally occurs in most matches.","Can create a 15% burst from a fully stocked trigger."],"cons":["Much weaker than its older version for passive token gain.","Competes with rescue perks that help ensure the unhook itself is safe.","Great Skill Check requirement adds execution risk."],"analysis":["Fast Track sits at this position because the live rework changed its identity from passive teammate-hook scaling into a personal rescue-to-objective converter. Each unhook grants one Token, and a later Great Skill Check turns those Tokens into permanent generator progress.","Fifteen percent permanent progress at three Tokens is a real swing. Permanent progress is especially valuable because regression cannot erase the charges that were removed from the generator's remaining requirement in the same way normal progress can be lost.","The catch is that you must personally generate the rescues and then land the Great Skill Check. A player who is chased often or loses rescue priority may struggle to build Tokens at all.","That lower consistency is why Fast Track no longer sits near its old ranking. The payoff is good, but the modern setup makes it a specialized objective perk instead of a broadly elite one."],"verdict":"A respectable rescue-to-generator conversion perk after its rework. Fast Track can create real permanent progress, but only if you personally earn the unhooks and land the Great.","publicationStatus":"published","tags":[],"queueRatingStatus":"reviewed","rankRange":null,"rankConfidence":"Not assessed","rankStatus":"inherited","evidenceStatus":"inherited","acquisition":{"type":"character","sourceCharacter":"Lee Yun-Jin"},"synergyPerkIds":["hyperfocus","deja-vu","well-make-it"],"synergyOther":[],"antiSynergyPerkIds":["stake-out"],"archetypeRatings":[],"reviewFlags":["v15-schema-migrated","queue-rating:normalized-tier-plus-v14-specialization-signal"],"synergies":["Hyperfocus","Déjà Vu","We'll Make It"],"antiSynergies":["Stake Out"],"name":"Fast Track","alternateName":null,"source":"Lee Yun-Jin","status":"Live 10.2.0","currentEffect":"Whenever you unhook another Survivor, you earn 1 Token, up to 1/2/3. While repairing a Generator, hitting a Great basic Skill Check spends all your Tokens; each Token spent grants that Generator 5% permanent progress.","activation":["You must unhook another Survivor to gain a Token.","You must be repairing a Generator and hit a Great basic Skill Check to spend Tokens.","Ends/deactivates when: Tokens are removed when spent on a Great basic repair Skill Check."],"patchNote":"Latest live balance change (9.6.0): Changed the trigger to your unhooks, capped the perk at 1/2/3 Tokens, and set progress to 5% per Token (from the prior rework's 1% live value).","plainEnglishSummary":"Your unhooks bank tokens that add permanent Generator progress when you hit a Great repair Skill Check.","cooldown":null,"duration":[],"tokenOrStackBehavior":"Gain 1 Token per Survivor you unhook, up to the tier cap of 1/2/3. A Great basic Skill Check while repairing spends all currently held Tokens; each spent Token grants 5% permanent Generator progress.","oncePerTrialOrOtherLimits":null,"statusEffectsInvolved":[],"specialInteractions":[],"sourceCharacter":"Lee Yun-Jin","isGeneralPerk":false,"currentLivePatchVerified":"10.2.0"},{"id":"wide-open-throttle","rank":77,"tier":"B","roles":["Chase","Pallet","Mobility"],"summary":"Fast-vault a Pallet to gain 15% Haste for 3 seconds, reset the Pallet upright, and block it for 60 seconds; cooldown is 60 seconds.","metaStatus":"Good","skillLevel":"High","soloQ":3,"swf":4,"unlockPriority":"Medium","glossaryKeys":["haste","looping"],"useCases":["Use a pallet vault as a short chase acceleration tool.","Reset a dropped pallet so the Killer cannot immediately interact with it normally during the blocked period.","Create a clearly marked temporary map state teammates can see."],"counters":["Only triggers on a fast Pallet vault.","The pallet becomes blocked for everyone for a full minute.","Fifteen percent Haste is much smaller than classic Exhaustion bursts."],"pros":["Can create chase distance without causing Exhaustion.","Unique pallet-state manipulation.","Visible blocked pallet helps team awareness."],"cons":["Long cooldown.","Can temporarily deny your own team access to the pallet.","Very map and path dependent."],"analysis":["Wide Open Throttle ranks this position because it offers a unique non-Exhaustion chase burst, but the pallet-reset mechanic is a double-edged sword. Fifteen percent Haste for three seconds is useful, yet far below the 50% burst provided by classic Exhaustion perks.","Resetting the pallet sounds powerful until the 60-second Entity block is considered. The resource exists again, but nobody can use it during the block, so the immediate value is mostly about changing the tile state and preventing a normal follow-up interaction.","Strong players can use the burst to leave the tile and potentially return after the block expires. The perk also avoids Exhaustion, allowing it to coexist with Lithe or another major chase perk.","The cooldown and awkward pallet lock keep it firmly mid-B. It is clever and sometimes strong, but not consistent enough to compete with straightforward chase tools."],"verdict":"An interesting non-Exhaustion pallet perk with real movement value and real awkwardness. Wide Open Throttle rewards planned transitions more than ordinary looping.","publicationStatus":"published","tags":["Haste"],"queueRatingStatus":"reviewed","rankRange":null,"rankConfidence":"Not assessed","rankStatus":"inherited","evidenceStatus":"inherited","acquisition":{"type":"character","sourceCharacter":"Shane Wiigwaas"},"synergyPerkIds":["lithe","finesse","five-moves-ahead"],"synergyOther":[],"antiSynergyPerkIds":[],"archetypeRatings":[],"reviewFlags":["v15-schema-migrated","queue-rating:normalized-tier-plus-v14-specialization-signal"],"synergies":["Lithe","Finesse","Five Moves Ahead"],"antiSynergies":[],"name":"Wide Open Throttle","alternateName":null,"source":"Shane Wiigwaas","status":"Live 10.2.0","currentEffect":"Fast-vaulting a Pallet grants 10/12.5/15% Haste for 3 seconds and immediately resets the Pallet upright; the Entity blocks it for 60 seconds, during which all Survivors see its Aura. Cooldown: 60 seconds.","activation":["Fast-vault a Pallet.","Ends/deactivates when: Haste ends after 3 seconds.","Ends/deactivates when: The Pallet block ends after 60 seconds.","Ends/deactivates when: Perk cannot be used again until the 60-second cooldown expires."],"patchNote":"Latest live balance change (10.0.1): Introduced with 10/12.5/15% Haste for 3 seconds, a 60-second pallet block with Aura visibility to all Survivors, and 60-second cooldown.","plainEnglishSummary":"Fast-vaulting a Pallet resets it, briefly speeds you up, and blocks that Pallet for a minute.","cooldown":"60 seconds","duration":["Haste: 3 seconds.","Pallet is blocked and its Aura shown to all Survivors for 60 seconds."],"tokenOrStackBehavior":null,"oncePerTrialOrOtherLimits":null,"statusEffectsInvolved":["Haste"],"specialInteractions":["The Pallet is reset upright and all Survivors see its Aura while it is blocked."],"sourceCharacter":"Shane Wiigwaas","isGeneralPerk":false,"currentLivePatchVerified":"10.2.0"},{"id":"ghost-notes","rank":78,"tier":"B","roles":["Exhaustion","Stealth","Recovery"],"summary":"While Exhausted, Scratch Marks disappear 50% faster and Exhaustion recovers up to 10% faster.","metaStatus":"Good","skillLevel":"Low","soloQ":3,"swf":3,"unlockPriority":"Medium","glossaryKeys":["exhausted","looping"],"useCases":["Pair with any Exhaustion perk to shorten downtime slightly.","Make trail tracking less reliable during the same period you are waiting for Exhaustion to recover.","Add passive value without changing activation habits."],"counters":["Does nothing while you are not Exhausted.","The 10% recovery increase is much smaller than Vigil.","Only changes Scratch-Mark duration, not Blood, sound, or Aura reading."],"pros":["Always passive once Exhausted.","Combines chase recovery and stealth.","Easy to use."],"cons":["Low numerical ceiling.","Requires another perk or effect to cause Exhaustion.","Usually worse than Vigil as pure Exhaustion support."],"analysis":["Ghost Notes lands at this position because it is a nice companion perk rather than a build centerpiece. While Exhausted, it slightly shortens the recovery period and makes Scratch Marks disappear much faster.","The stealth half is often more interesting than the recovery number. Fifty percent faster Scratch-Mark disappearance can make long chase transitions harder to read, particularly after an Exhaustion burst creates enough distance to break line of sight.","The problem is efficiency. Ten percent faster Exhaustion recovery is helpful but modest, and Vigil offers a stronger support effect that can also help nearby teammates.","Ghost Notes therefore makes sense when the user specifically wants the combination of Exhaustion support and trail disruption. As a general slot, its impact is too small for the upper tiers."],"verdict":"A useful but modest Exhaustion companion. Ghost Notes adds passive trail disruption and a little recovery speed, but rarely changes a match by itself.","publicationStatus":"published","tags":[],"queueRatingStatus":"reviewed","rankRange":null,"rankConfidence":"Not assessed","rankStatus":"inherited","evidenceStatus":"inherited","acquisition":{"type":"character","sourceCharacter":"Vee Boonyasak"},"synergyPerkIds":["sprint-burst","lithe","dead-hard","vigil"],"synergyOther":[],"antiSynergyPerkIds":[],"archetypeRatings":[],"reviewFlags":["v15-schema-migrated","queue-rating:normalized-tier-plus-v14-specialization-signal"],"synergies":["Sprint Burst","Lithe","Dead Hard","Vigil"],"antiSynergies":[],"name":"Ghost Notes","alternateName":null,"source":"Vee Boonyasak","status":"Live 10.2.0","currentEffect":"While you are Exhausted, your Scratch Marks disappear 50% faster and your Exhaustion recovery rate increases by 5/7.5/10%. Ghost Notes does not itself cause Exhaustion.","activation":["You must be suffering from the Exhausted status effect.","Ends/deactivates when: The effects stop when Exhausted ends."],"patchNote":"Latest live balance change (9.2.0): Introduced; no later material live balance change located in the official notes checked.","plainEnglishSummary":"While Exhausted, you recover from it faster and your Scratch Marks fade faster.","cooldown":null,"duration":["Applies for as long as you are Exhausted."],"tokenOrStackBehavior":null,"oncePerTrialOrOtherLimits":null,"statusEffectsInvolved":["Exhausted"],"specialInteractions":["Ghost Notes does not inflict Exhausted; it only affects an existing Exhausted status."],"sourceCharacter":"Vee Boonyasak","isGeneralPerk":false,"currentLivePatchVerified":"10.2.0"},{"id":"cross-examination","rank":79,"tier":"B","roles":["Information","Stealth","Chase"],"summary":"While in the Killer's Terror Radius and not being chased, follow their Light Marks to gain Elusive, which lingers for 3/4/5 seconds after leaving the marks.","metaStatus":"Good","skillLevel":"Medium–High","soloQ":3,"swf":3,"unlockPriority":"Medium","glossaryKeys":["aura-reading","looping"],"useCases":["Track the Killer's recent path around obstructed structures through persistent Light Marks.","Step across a Mark to gain short Elusive protection before changing route.","Use trail information on indoor maps where direct line of sight is frequently broken."],"counters":["The Killer must satisfy the perk's proximity condition for Marks to be produced.","Marks last only 10 seconds.","The Elusive window is brief and still requires the Survivor to physically reach a Mark.","It does not generate its tracking value while you are being chased by the Killer."],"pros":["Provides a unique trail-based way to track Killer movement.","Can turn the Killer's own path into a short stealth resource.","New information type can remain useful when ordinary Aura reading is blocked."],"cons":["Less intuitive than standard Aura-reading perks.","Short Elusive duration.","Value is highly dependent on geometry and proximity."],"analysis":["Cross-Examination lands at this position because its new Light Mark mechanic offers a distinctive kind of Killer tracking. Rather than simply revealing an Aura, it leaves a recent movement trail that can persist around corners and through complicated structures, giving the Survivor clues about where the Killer just traveled.","The second half creates the more interesting decision. Walking over a Light Mark grants a brief Elusive window, allowing the Survivor to suppress several tracking channels while repositioning. In the right indoor tile, that can turn the Killer's own movement history into a stealth route.","The perk is still young in 10.1.2a, so we are deliberately conservative. Its usefulness depends on learning how Marks spawn, reading them quickly, and having geometry where the information changes a decision. A simple Aura read is easier to interpret for most players.","That learning curve and the short Elusive duration keep it in B for now. There is enough utility and originality here to deserve a respectable position, but it should earn a higher ranking through sustained live performance rather than novelty."],"verdict":"A promising tracking-and-stealth hybrid. Cross-Examination can be clever and powerful around complex geometry, but its young meta and short protection window justify caution.","publicationStatus":"published","tags":["Tracking"],"queueRatingStatus":"reviewed","rankRange":null,"rankConfidence":"Not assessed","rankStatus":"inherited","evidenceStatus":"inherited","acquisition":{"type":"character","sourceCharacter":"Shane Wiigwaas"},"synergyPerkIds":["iron-will","lightweight","fixated","quick-quiet"],"synergyOther":[],"antiSynergyPerkIds":[],"archetypeRatings":[],"reviewFlags":["v15-schema-migrated","queue-rating:normalized-tier-plus-v14-specialization-signal"],"synergies":["Iron Will","Lightweight","Fixated","Quick & Quiet"],"antiSynergies":[],"name":"Cross-Examination","alternateName":null,"source":"Shane Wiigwaas","status":"Live 10.2.0","currentEffect":"While you are in the Killer's Terror Radius and not being chased by the Killer, the Killer leaves Light Marks that last 10 seconds and that you can see. While on the Killer's Light Marks, you gain Elusive; this ends after 3/4/5 seconds.","activation":["Be inside the Killer's Terror Radius.","Not be chased by the Killer.","Stand on a visible Light Mark to gain Elusive.","Ends/deactivates when: Light Marks are not generated for you while you are being chased or outside the Terror Radius.","Ends/deactivates when: Light Marks expire after 10 seconds; Elusive ends 3/4/5 seconds after you leave the Light Marks."],"patchNote":"Latest live balance change (10.0.3): Added the requirement that you are not being chased by the Killer (perk introduced in 10.0.1).","plainEnglishSummary":"While in the Killer's Terror Radius and not in chase, standing on the Killer's Light Marks grants you a brief Elusive effect.","cooldown":null,"duration":["Light Marks: 10 seconds.","Elusive: 3/4/5 seconds by tier."],"tokenOrStackBehavior":null,"oncePerTrialOrOtherLimits":null,"statusEffectsInvolved":["Elusive"],"specialInteractions":[],"sourceCharacter":"Shane Wiigwaas","isGeneralPerk":false,"currentLivePatchVerified":"10.2.0"},{"id":"strength-in-shadows","rank":80,"tier":"B","roles":["Healing","Self-Sustain","Information"],"summary":"In the Basement, self-heal at 70% normal speed; completing the heal reveals the Killer for up to 10 seconds.","metaStatus":"Good","skillLevel":"Low–Medium","soloQ":3,"swf":3,"unlockPriority":"Medium","glossaryKeys":["reset","aura-reading","health-state"],"useCases":["Create independent self-sustain when teammates are unavailable.","Use the post-heal Killer Aura read to decide how to leave the Basement safely.","Pair with Basement-adjacent objectives or perks that already bring you downstairs."],"counters":["Requires traveling into the Basement.","Basement positioning can be dangerous if the Killer checks it.","A teammate heal elsewhere may be faster overall."],"pros":["Much faster than Self-Care.","Includes a long Killer Aura read after completion.","No Med-Kit required."],"cons":["Location tax is significant.","Can walk into a dangerous dead zone to activate.","Travel time can erase the apparent healing efficiency."],"analysis":["Strength in Shadows earns this position because 70% normal healing speed is a respectable independent self-heal, much faster than base Self-Care. The ten-second Killer Aura read afterward also reduces some of the danger of leaving the Basement.","The real cost is travel. A perk can quote a good heal time and still be inefficient if the Survivor spends fifteen seconds running downstairs and back out. Maps with centrally accessible Basements are kinder than maps where the trip is a major detour.","The perk becomes better when the build or match already gives you a reason to visit the Basement. In those cases, the activation cost shrinks and the self-sustain feels much more efficient.","It stays in B because geography is unavoidable. The effect is strong enough to respect, but the Basement requirement prevents it from competing with more portable healing tools."],"verdict":"A good independent heal with a real map tax. Strength in Shadows is efficient once you are downstairs, but getting there is part of the perk's true cost.","publicationStatus":"published","tags":[],"queueRatingStatus":"reviewed","rankRange":null,"rankConfidence":"Not assessed","rankStatus":"inherited","evidenceStatus":"inherited","acquisition":{"type":"character","sourceCharacter":"Sable Ward"},"synergyPerkIds":["botany-knowledge","wicked","inner-strength","iron-will"],"synergyOther":[],"antiSynergyPerkIds":[],"archetypeRatings":[],"reviewFlags":["v15-schema-migrated","queue-rating:normalized-tier-plus-v14-specialization-signal"],"synergies":["Botany Knowledge","Wicked","Inner Strength","Iron Will"],"antiSynergies":[],"name":"Strength in Shadows","alternateName":null,"source":"Sable Ward","status":"Live 10.2.0","currentEffect":"While inside the Basement, unlocks self-healing without a Med-Kit at 70% of normal Healing speed. After completing a heal in the Basement, reveals the Killer's Aura to you for 6/8/10 seconds.","activation":["Be inside the Basement to use the self-heal ability.","Complete the heal while in the Basement to reveal the Killer's Aura.","Ends/deactivates when: The self-heal ability is available only while inside the Basement.","Ends/deactivates when: Aura reveal ends after 6/8/10 seconds."],"patchNote":"Latest live balance change (unknown): No material live balance change could be verified from available patch history.","plainEnglishSummary":"Lets you self-heal at reduced speed in the Basement and then briefly reveals the Killer after the heal.","cooldown":null,"duration":["Killer Aura reveal: 6/8/10 seconds after completing the Basement heal."],"tokenOrStackBehavior":null,"oncePerTrialOrOtherLimits":null,"statusEffectsInvolved":[],"specialInteractions":["The self-heal does not require a Med-Kit."],"sourceCharacter":"Sable Ward","isGeneralPerk":false,"currentLivePatchVerified":"10.2.0"},{"id":"bound-by-obsession","rank":81,"tier":"B","roles":["Information","Objective","Utility"],"summary":"Whenever the Killer sees your Aura, see theirs back and gain up to 10% speed to repairs, healing, and Totem interactions; the Obsession exposes their Aura every 30 seconds.","metaStatus":"Good","skillLevel":"High","soloQ":3,"swf":4,"unlockPriority":"Medium","glossaryKeys":["aura-reading"],"useCases":["Turn Killer Aura-reading perks into reciprocal information.","Use the periodic Obsession reveal to gain repeated Killer Aura windows.","Exploit the temporary 8/9/10% action-speed boost while the Aura interaction is active."],"counters":["The Killer also sees you during the scheduled Obsession reveal.","Aura-blocking and Undetectable can reduce the information exchange.","The periodic reveal can be dangerous when you are already vulnerable."],"pros":["Punishes Aura-heavy Killer builds with reciprocal information.","Provides a small action-speed bonus during reveal windows.","Can intentionally feed We See You tokens."],"cons":["High-risk periodic reveal.","Much less appealing for stealth-oriented players.","Value depends on Killer Aura-reading behavior."],"analysis":["Bound by Obsession gained a meaningful numerical upgrade in 10.2. The reciprocal Aura mechanic remains, but the action-speed bonus during those windows now reaches 10% and includes blessing as well as cleansing, healing, and repairing.","As Obsession, the periodic reveal now lasts four seconds. That creates a predictable information trade: the Killer sees you, you see them, and you gain a short burst of productive action speed if you are working at the time.","The risk is still real. Sometimes the Killer benefits more from knowing your location than you benefit from seeing theirs, especially if the reveal occurs while you are vulnerable.","The buff improves the reward side of that trade enough that the perk deserves reconsideration upward, particularly in confident information-heavy builds."],"verdict":"A stronger reciprocal-Aura perk in 10.2. The danger remains, but 10% action speed and four-second periodic reads make the reward much more credible.","publicationStatus":"published","reviewFlags":["10.2-live-change","v15-schema-migrated","rank-review-applied","queue-rating:normalized-tier-plus-v14-specialization-signal"],"tags":["Obsession"],"queueRatingStatus":"reviewed","rankRange":[72,90],"rankConfidence":"Medium","rankStatus":"stable","evidenceStatus":"inherited","acquisition":{"type":"general","sourceCharacter":"General"},"synergyPerkIds":["we-see-you","distortion","resilience","deja-vu"],"synergyOther":[],"antiSynergyPerkIds":[],"archetypeRatings":[],"synergies":["We See You","Distortion","Resilience","Déjà Vu"],"antiSynergies":[],"name":"Bound by Obsession","alternateName":null,"source":"General perk","status":"Live 10.2.0","currentEffect":"Whenever the Killer sees your Aura, you see the Killer's Aura. While the Killer sees your Aura, you Bless and Cleanse Totems, heal, and repair 8/9/10% faster. While you are the Obsession, every 30 seconds the Killer sees your Aura for 4 seconds. At Trial start, you are more likely to become the Obsession.","activation":["The mutual Aura and action-speed effects activate whenever the Killer sees your Aura.","If you are the Obsession, the Killer sees your Aura every 30 seconds.","Ends/deactivates when: The mutual Aura and action-speed effects end when the Killer stops seeing your Aura.","Ends/deactivates when: Each periodic Obsession Aura reveal lasts 4 seconds."],"patchNote":"Latest live balance change (10.2.0): Increased periodic Obsession Aura reveal from 3 to 4 seconds and increased the linked action-speed bonus from 2/4/6% to 8/9/10%, adding Blessing to the affected Totem actions.","plainEnglishSummary":"When the Killer can read your Aura, you can read theirs and perform several actions faster; as the Obsession, you periodically reveal yourself to the Killer.","cooldown":null,"duration":["Obsession Aura reveal: 4 seconds every 30 seconds."],"tokenOrStackBehavior":null,"oncePerTrialOrOtherLimits":null,"statusEffectsInvolved":[],"specialInteractions":["The 8/9/10% bonus applies to Blessing, Cleansing, Healing, and Repairing while the Killer sees your Aura.","At Trial start, you are more likely to be selected as the Obsession."],"sourceCharacter":"General","isGeneralPerk":true,"currentLivePatchVerified":"10.2.0"},{"id":"one-two-three-four","rank":82,"tier":"B","roles":["Team Support","Skill Check"],"summary":"Perform while idle to empower nearby Survivors; the completed performance can increase basic Skill Check frequency for healing and repair for a long duration.","metaStatus":"Good","skillLevel":"Medium","soloQ":3,"swf":4,"unlockPriority":"Medium","glossaryKeys":["swf","pressure"],"useCases":["Support Hyperfocus or Autodidact-style builds that want more Skill Checks.","Set up a team buff before a long repair or healing phase.","Use the performance Aura to signal your support location to nearby teammates."],"counters":["Requires stopping to perform.","The benefit is specialized around Skill Check frequency.","Poor team positioning can waste the nearby empowerment."],"pros":["Unique team Skill Check support.","Can last well beyond the performance.","Synergizes with several high-ceiling perks."],"cons":["Setup time.","Niche payoff.","Much weaker for teammates whose builds do not care about extra Skill Checks."],"analysis":["One-Two-Three-Four! ranks this position because it supports a very specific but legitimate class of builds. Hyperfocus and Autodidact both become stronger when more Skill Checks appear, so a perk that manipulates frequency can amplify their ceilings.","The performance mechanic is the opportunity cost. The user must stop what they are doing and spend time setting up the buff rather than repairing, healing, or moving to a rescue.","The effect also depends on nearby team composition. A random teammate running ordinary perks may gain little from extra Skill Checks, while a coordinated Hyperfocus setup can deliberately exploit them.","That narrow synergy keeps the perk in mid-B. It can be valuable in an intentional build, but is not something most loadouts want by default."],"verdict":"A specialized Skill Check support perk. One-Two-Three-Four! can make high-ceiling generator and healing builds better, but only after deliberate setup.","publicationStatus":"published","tags":["Support","Team"],"queueRatingStatus":"reviewed","rankRange":null,"rankConfidence":"Not assessed","rankStatus":"inherited","evidenceStatus":"inherited","acquisition":{"type":"character","sourceCharacter":"Vee Boonyasak"},"synergyPerkIds":["hyperfocus","autodidact","prove-thyself"],"synergyOther":[],"antiSynergyPerkIds":[],"archetypeRatings":[],"reviewFlags":["v15-schema-migrated","queue-rating:normalized-tier-plus-v14-specialization-signal"],"synergies":["Hyperfocus","Autodidact","Prove Thyself"],"antiSynergies":[],"name":"One-Two-Three-Four!","alternateName":null,"source":"Vee Boonyasak","status":"Live 10.2.0","currentEffect":"While standing and idle, press Active Ability 2 to begin a Performance lasting up to 15 seconds. It empowers Survivors within 16 metres and generates continuous Skill Checks during the Performance. If you complete the Performance, empowered Survivors receive a 90-second effect while Healing or Repairing that increases Skill Check occurrence chance by 20%. Cancelling or completing the Performance starts a 110/100/90-second cooldown by tier.","activation":["Be standing and idle.","Press Active Ability 2 when the perk is off cooldown.","Ends/deactivates when: The Performance ends after at most 15 seconds or when cancelled.","Ends/deactivates when: The post-Performance benefit is granted only if the Performance is completed and lasts 90 seconds."],"patchNote":"Latest live balance change (9.2.0): Introduced; no later material live balance change located in the official notes checked.","plainEnglishSummary":"A completed Performance gives nearby Survivors more frequent Healing and Repair Skill Checks for 90 seconds.","cooldown":"110/100/90 seconds after cancelling or completing the Performance.","duration":["Performance: up to 15 seconds.","Empowered area: 16 metres from your location during the Performance.","Skill Check chance bonus: 90 seconds after a completed Performance."],"tokenOrStackBehavior":null,"oncePerTrialOrOtherLimits":null,"statusEffectsInvolved":[],"specialInteractions":["The 9.2.0 live patch fixed an issue where the effect stacked with other Survivors using One-Two-Three-Four!, so duplicate copies do not stack."],"sourceCharacter":"Vee Boonyasak","isGeneralPerk":false,"currentLivePatchVerified":"10.2.0"},{"id":"better-than-new","rank":83,"tier":"B","roles":["Healing","Team Support"],"summary":"After you finish healing someone, they heal, bless/cleanse, and unlock Chests up to 50% faster until they take damage.","metaStatus":"Good","skillLevel":"Low","soloQ":3,"swf":4,"unlockPriority":"Medium–High","glossaryKeys":["reset","health-state"],"useCases":["Turn one completed heal into a strong support buff on that teammate.","Create a fast healer who can immediately help reset someone else.","Buff a teammate before they work through Hexes, Boons, or chest interactions."],"counters":["The buff disappears as soon as the affected Survivor takes damage.","It does not increase generator repair speed.","You must first complete a full heal on someone else."],"pros":["Up to 50% is a major support-speed bonus.","No cooldown after the initial heal trigger.","10.2 massively improved the live numbers."],"cons":["Target loses everything on the next hit.","No direct chase protection.","Value depends on the healed teammate actually using the supported actions."],"analysis":["Better Than New is one of the clearest 10.2 winners. The old 16% ceiling became 50% for healing, Totem interactions, and Chest unlocking, which is finally large enough to shape team decisions.","The best use is chaining support. Heal an injured teammate, then let that newly buffed Survivor perform the next heal dramatically faster while you return to another task.","The effect is fragile because one hit removes it, and generator repair is not part of the speed package. A Killer applying broad injury pressure can therefore erase value quickly.","Even with those limits, the old low-tier reputation is obsolete. The independent ranking review should treat the 10.2 version as a serious support perk rather than legacy filler."],"verdict":"A legitimate support perk after a huge 10.2 buff. Fifty percent faster healing and side-objective actions gives the healed Survivor something worth protecting.","publicationStatus":"published","reviewFlags":["10.2-live-change","v15-schema-migrated","queue-rating:normalized-tier-plus-v14-specialization-signal"],"tags":["Support","Action Speed"],"queueRatingStatus":"reviewed","rankRange":null,"rankConfidence":"Not assessed","rankStatus":"inherited","evidenceStatus":"inherited","acquisition":{"type":"character","sourceCharacter":"Rebecca Chambers"},"synergyPerkIds":["botany-knowledge","empathic-connection","desperate-measures"],"synergyOther":["Boon perks"],"antiSynergyPerkIds":[],"archetypeRatings":[],"synergies":["Botany Knowledge","Empathic Connection","Desperate Measures","Boon perks"],"antiSynergies":[],"name":"Better Than New","alternateName":null,"source":"Rebecca Chambers","status":"Live 10.2.0","currentEffect":"Whenever you finish healing another Survivor, until they take damage, they Bless and Cleanse Totems, heal, and unlock Chests 40/45/50% faster.","activation":["Finish healing another Survivor.","Ends/deactivates when: The affected Survivor loses the bonuses when they take damage."],"patchNote":"Latest live balance change (10.2.0): Increased the affected Survivor's Blessing/Cleansing, healing, and Chest-unlocking speed bonuses from 12/14/16% to 40/45/50%.","plainEnglishSummary":"Finishing a heal gives that Survivor faster Totem interactions, healing, and Chest unlocking until they take damage.","cooldown":null,"duration":["Persists on the healed Survivor until they take damage."],"tokenOrStackBehavior":null,"oncePerTrialOrOtherLimits":null,"statusEffectsInvolved":[],"specialInteractions":["The bonuses apply to the Survivor you finished healing, not to you."],"sourceCharacter":"Rebecca Chambers","isGeneralPerk":false,"currentLivePatchVerified":"10.2.0"},{"id":"blood-rush","rank":84,"tier":"B","roles":["Anti-Tunnel","Exhaustion","Chase"],"summary":"After an unhook, gain a limited window where you can instantly clear an existing Exhausted status once, potentially bringing a powerful Exhaustion perk back online.","metaStatus":"Good","skillLevel":"High","soloQ":3,"swf":4,"unlockPriority":"High","glossaryKeys":["exhausted","anti-tunnel","tunneling","conspicuous-action"],"useCases":["Reset Sprint Burst, Lithe, Dead Hard, or another Exhaustion perk during the dangerous post-unhook window.","Turn an expected tunnel chase into a second Exhaustion-perk activation the Killer may not be prepared for.","Use the threat of another chase burst to reach a safer area after rescue."],"counters":["Only activates after an unhook and expires after the short activation window.","Conspicuous Actions end the opportunity early.","It is disabled once the Exit Gates are powered."],"pros":["Can effectively create a second use of an elite chase perk.","Excellent anti-tunnel ceiling.","No health-state sacrifice in its modern form."],"cons":["Requires already being Exhausted.","Very timing-sensitive.","Completely inactive before your first unhook."],"analysis":["Blood Rush leads this band because resetting Exhaustion is one of the more powerful effects a Survivor perk can offer. Exhaustion perks are deliberately limited by downtime, so removing that downtime during the most dangerous post-unhook portion of the match can radically change a tunnel chase.","The strongest use is not random activation. It is planning around a specific second chase tool. A Survivor who used Sprint Burst before going down, or who needs Dead Hard available again after rescue, can create a second layer of chase protection that the Killer may not expect.","The perk also improved significantly from its older, harsher form. It no longer requires sacrificing a health state to clear Exhaustion, which makes the current version much more practical as anti-tunnel utility rather than a desperation gimmick.","It remains B because the activation is narrow and temporary. You must be unhooked, already Exhausted, and able to use the reset before a Conspicuous Action or the timer ends. When those pieces line up, Blood Rush can perform above this rank."],"verdict":"A high-ceiling post-unhook Exhaustion reset. Blood Rush is narrow, but when paired with an elite Exhaustion perk it can make a tunnel chase unexpectedly expensive.","publicationStatus":"published","tags":[],"queueRatingStatus":"reviewed","rankRange":null,"rankConfidence":"Not assessed","rankStatus":"inherited","evidenceStatus":"inherited","acquisition":{"type":"character","sourceCharacter":"Renato Lyra"},"synergyPerkIds":["sprint-burst","dead-hard","lithe","off-the-record"],"synergyOther":[],"antiSynergyPerkIds":[],"archetypeRatings":[],"reviewFlags":["v15-schema-migrated","queue-rating:normalized-tier-plus-v14-specialization-signal"],"synergies":["Sprint Burst","Dead Hard","Lithe","Off the Record"],"antiSynergies":[],"name":"Blood Rush","alternateName":null,"source":"Renato Lyra","status":"Live 10.2.0","currentEffect":"After being unhooked by any means, the perk activates for 40/50/60 seconds. While active, use the Active Ability button to instantly recover from an existing Exhausted status. It does not cause Exhausted. A Conspicuous Action ends it early; using it deactivates it, and it is disabled for the rest of the Trial once the Exit Gates are powered.","activation":["Be unhooked by any means.","Use the Active Ability while Exhausted during the activation window.","Ends/deactivates when: A Conspicuous Action ends it early.","Ends/deactivates when: It deactivates after use and is disabled once Exit Gates are powered."],"patchNote":"Latest live balance change (8.3.0): Reworked into the current post-unhook Exhausted-removal effect.","plainEnglishSummary":"After an unhook, use a limited window to remove Exhausted once without receiving Exhausted again.","cooldown":null,"duration":["Activation window: 40/50/60 seconds by tier."],"tokenOrStackBehavior":null,"oncePerTrialOrOtherLimits":"Once used, deactivates; disabled for remainder of Trial when Exit Gates are powered.","statusEffectsInvolved":["Exhausted"],"specialInteractions":["Blood Rush itself does not cause Exhausted."],"sourceCharacter":"Renato Lyra","isGeneralPerk":false,"currentLivePatchVerified":"10.2.0"},{"id":"empathic-connection","rank":85,"tier":"B","roles":["Healing","Team Support"],"summary":"Heal other Survivors substantially faster, while every injured teammate can see your Aura anywhere on the map.","metaStatus":"Good","skillLevel":"Low","soloQ":3,"swf":3,"unlockPriority":"High","glossaryKeys":["reset","solo-q","aura-reading","health-state"],"useCases":["Act as a visible healing anchor for injured teammates in Solo Q.","Shorten normal team resets without needing a trigger or token.","Let injured teammates come to you instead of wasting time searching for each other."],"counters":["The healing bonus only applies when you heal someone else.","Your visible Aura can draw multiple teammates away from generators if they over-prioritize resets.","You gain no personal self-heal speed."],"pros":["Always-on healing bonus.","Map-wide injured-teammate coordination.","Very easy to use."],"cons":["No chase value.","Can encourage unnecessary healing.","Less impactful if the team already has strong voice communication."],"analysis":["Empathic Connection ranks this position because it combines two support effects that naturally reinforce each other. Injured Survivors can see your Aura from anywhere, and when they reach you, your healing speed is significantly increased.","That solves a real Solo Q problem: injured players frequently spend time searching for someone willing to reset them. With Empathic Connection, the support player becomes a visible destination instead of an uncertain possibility.","The perk is also clean. There is no hook trigger, token stack, or proximity requirement for the Aura. If someone is injured, they know where you are. If you heal them, the speed bonus applies.","It stays in B because healing support does not matter in every game state. Strong teams often need to stay on generators while injured, and SWF can coordinate heal locations verbally. The perk is excellent at its role without being a universal slot."],"verdict":"A very clean Solo Q support perk. Empathic Connection makes you easy to find and meaningfully faster at the job teammates are seeking you out to perform.","publicationStatus":"published","reviewFlags":["10.2-live-change","v15-schema-migrated","queue-rating:normalized-tier-plus-v14-specialization-signal"],"tags":["Support","Team"],"queueRatingStatus":"reviewed","rankRange":null,"rankConfidence":"Not assessed","rankStatus":"inherited","evidenceStatus":"inherited","acquisition":{"type":"character","sourceCharacter":"Yoichi Asakawa"},"synergyPerkIds":["botany-knowledge","autodidact","desperate-measures","aftercare"],"synergyOther":[],"antiSynergyPerkIds":[],"archetypeRatings":[],"synergies":["Botany Knowledge","Autodidact","Desperate Measures","Aftercare"],"antiSynergies":[],"name":"Empathic Connection","alternateName":null,"source":"Yoichi Asakawa","status":"Live 10.2.0","currentEffect":"You heal other Survivors 30/35/40% faster. Injured Survivors see your Aura.","activation":["The healing-speed bonus applies while healing another Survivor.","The Aura effect applies to injured Survivors.","Ends/deactivates when: The Aura effect ends for a Survivor when they are no longer injured."],"patchNote":"Latest live balance change (10.2.0): Increased altruistic healing-speed bonus from 25/30/35% to 30/35/40%; injured Survivors continue to see your Aura.","plainEnglishSummary":"You heal teammates faster and injured teammates can see your Aura.","cooldown":null,"duration":["Healing-speed bonus is passive during altruistic healing.","Aura visibility applies while another Survivor is injured."],"tokenOrStackBehavior":null,"oncePerTrialOrOtherLimits":null,"statusEffectsInvolved":[],"specialInteractions":[],"sourceCharacter":"Yoichi Asakawa","isGeneralPerk":false,"currentLivePatchVerified":"10.2.0"},{"id":"leader","rank":86,"tier":"B","roles":["Team Support","Healing"],"summary":"Nearby teammates perform several non-generator actions 30% faster, including healing, unhooking, sabotaging, cleansing, unlocking, and opening Exit Gates.","metaStatus":"Good","skillLevel":"Low","soloQ":3,"swf":4,"unlockPriority":"High","glossaryKeys":["swf","reset","hook-state"],"useCases":["Speed up a teammate healing you without needing to equip a personal healing-speed perk.","Accelerate endgame gate opening and contested unhooks.","Support sabotage and cleansing plays when teammates are operating nearby."],"counters":["You do not benefit from your own Leader.","Teammates must be nearby to receive the effect.","It does not increase generator repair speed."],"pros":["Broad action-speed package.","Thirty percent is substantial.","Linger keeps the buff active briefly after leaving range."],"cons":["No self-benefit.","Requires proximity.","Excludes generator repair."],"analysis":["Leader takes this position because thirty percent faster action speed across several important interactions is a strong support package. Healing, unhooking, gate opening, cleansing, sabotage, and chest interactions all occur often enough that the perk can find value throughout a match.","The most practical interaction is often a teammate healing you. Because the perk owner cannot benefit from Leader directly, the value appears when another Survivor performs the action near you. That design makes it more naturally supportive than self-sufficient.","Endgame is another strong phase. Faster gate opening and unhooking can matter enormously under pressure, and the brief linger means teammates can begin the interaction near you without remaining attached to your position for the entire duration.","Leader stays in B because its strongest effects depend on another Survivor being nearby and performing the right action. It is broad but not individually empowering, which is why coordinated groups usually get more from it than isolated Solo Q players."],"verdict":"A strong general support aura with a meaningful 30% bonus. Leader does many useful things, but always through someone else.","publicationStatus":"published","tags":["Support","Action Speed","Team"],"queueRatingStatus":"reviewed","rankRange":null,"rankConfidence":"Not assessed","rankStatus":"inherited","evidenceStatus":"inherited","acquisition":{"type":"character","sourceCharacter":"Dwight Fairfield"},"synergyPerkIds":["prove-thyself","bond","no-one-left-behind","well-make-it"],"synergyOther":[],"antiSynergyPerkIds":[],"archetypeRatings":[],"reviewFlags":["v15-schema-migrated","queue-rating:normalized-tier-plus-v14-specialization-signal"],"synergies":["Prove Thyself","Bond","No One Left Behind","We'll Make It"],"antiSynergies":[],"name":"Leader","alternateName":null,"source":"Dwight Fairfield","status":"Live 10.2.0","currentEffect":"All other Survivors within 10 m of you gain 20/25/30% action speed for Cleansing, Gate-Opening, Healing, Sabotaging, Unhooking, and Unlocking. The effect lingers for 15 seconds after leaving the radius. A Survivor can be affected by only one instance of Leader at a time; the perk owner does not benefit from their own Leader.","activation":["Another Survivor must be within 10 m of you to receive the action-speed bonus.","Ends/deactivates when: For each affected Survivor, the bonus ends 15 seconds after leaving the 10 m radius."],"patchNote":"Latest live balance change (9.2.0): Raised the action-speed bonus to 20/25/30% from 15/20/25% and increased the radius to 10 m from 8 m.","plainEnglishSummary":"Nearby teammates gain faster listed actions, with the bonus lingering briefly after they leave your radius.","cooldown":null,"duration":["Linger after leaving range: 15 seconds."],"tokenOrStackBehavior":null,"oncePerTrialOrOtherLimits":"Each Survivor can benefit from only one instance of Leader at a time.","statusEffectsInvolved":[],"specialInteractions":["The perk affects other Survivors, not its owner."],"sourceCharacter":"Dwight Fairfield","isGeneralPerk":false,"currentLivePatchVerified":"10.2.0"},{"id":"wake-up","rank":87,"tier":"B","roles":["Endgame","Information"],"summary":"After all generators are completed, reveal Exit Gates, show teammates your Aura while opening one, and open it up to 70% faster with all four Survivors alive.","metaStatus":"Good","skillLevel":"Low","soloQ":4,"swf":3,"unlockPriority":"Medium–High","glossaryKeys":["aura-reading","pressure"],"useCases":["Locate either Exit Gate immediately on indoor or visually confusing maps.","Open a gate much faster while several Survivors remain alive.","Broadcast which gate you are opening so teammates can route toward it."],"counters":["Provides absolutely no value before all generators are completed.","The speed bonus shrinks as Survivors die.","A match that never reaches powered gates leaves the perk completely unused."],"pros":["Up to 70% faster gate opening is a major endgame time save.","Global gate information removes navigation uncertainty.","Built-in teammate Aura communication helps Solo Q."],"cons":["Dead for the entire pre-endgame phase.","Cannot help the team reach the point where it activates.","Less powerful when few Survivors remain alive."],"analysis":["Wake Up! became even more explosive at a healthy-team endgame. Tier III now gives 10% base gate speed plus another 20% for each other Survivor alive, reaching 70% faster opening with all four Survivors still in the Trial.","That is enough to materially change Killer rotation math. A gate that would normally remain contestable can become nearly finished before the Killer completes a cross-map check.","The information package remains helpful as well: you see Gate Switches and teammates see your Aura while you are opening one, reducing endgame confusion in Solo Q.","The same structural weakness remains absolute. Wake Up! does nothing before all generators are completed. Its live numbers warrant a higher review, but its dead early game still prevents a universal recommendation."],"verdict":"A monstrous gate opener in a four-Survivor endgame, now reaching 70% faster. Wake Up! is still dead before the generators finish, but its active payoff is no joke.","publicationStatus":"published","reviewFlags":["10.2-live-change","v15-schema-migrated","queue-rating:audit-partial-plus-normalized"],"tags":["Exit Gate"],"queueRatingStatus":"reviewed","rankRange":null,"rankConfidence":"Not assessed","rankStatus":"inherited","evidenceStatus":"inherited","acquisition":{"type":"character","sourceCharacter":"Quentin Smith"},"synergyPerkIds":["hope","adrenaline","no-one-left-behind","down-to-the-last"],"synergyOther":[],"antiSynergyPerkIds":[],"archetypeRatings":[],"synergies":["Hope","Adrenaline","No One Left Behind","Down to the Last"],"antiSynergies":[],"name":"Wake Up!","alternateName":null,"source":"Quentin Smith","status":"Live 10.2.0","currentEffect":"When all Generators are completed, you see the Auras of Exit Gate Switches. While opening an Exit Gate, other Survivors see your Aura. You open Exit Gates 8/9/10% faster, plus an additional 20% faster for each other Survivor alive.","activation":["All Generators must be completed.","The self-Aura sharing and speed bonus apply while you are opening an Exit Gate.","Ends/deactivates when: Exit Gate Switch Aura reading remains available after all Generators are completed.","Ends/deactivates when: Your Aura is shared only while opening an Exit Gate."],"patchNote":"Latest live balance change (10.2.0): Changed Exit Gate opening speed to 8/9/10% plus 20% for each other Survivor alive (was 8/10/12.5% per any Survivor alive); Exit Gate Switch and self-Aura information retained.","plainEnglishSummary":"After all Generators are done, Exit Gate Switches are revealed, teammates can see you opening a Gate, and your Gate-opening speed scales with other living Survivors.","cooldown":null,"duration":["Exit Gate Switch Aura reveal persists after all Generators are completed.","Your Aura is shared while opening an Exit Gate."],"tokenOrStackBehavior":null,"oncePerTrialOrOtherLimits":null,"statusEffectsInvolved":[],"specialInteractions":["Gate-opening speed is 8/9/10% plus 20% for each other Survivor alive."],"sourceCharacter":"Quentin Smith","isGeneralPerk":false,"currentLivePatchVerified":"10.2.0"},{"id":"no-one-left-behind","rank":88,"tier":"B","roles":["Endgame","Rescue","Healing"],"summary":"Once the Exit Gates are powered, see every teammate, heal and unhook up to 100% faster, and give Survivors you unhook 20% Haste for 10 seconds.","metaStatus":"Good","skillLevel":"Low","soloQ":4,"swf":4,"unlockPriority":"High","glossaryKeys":["hook-state","haste","aura-reading","health-state"],"useCases":["Turn a dangerous endgame hook into a much faster rescue interaction.","Use global teammate Auras to understand who is at gates, hooked, injured, or moving for a save.","Give the rescued Survivor a huge 20% Haste window to reach safety."],"counters":["Does absolutely nothing before the Exit Gates are powered.","A match that collapses before endgame leaves the slot dead.","Endgame Killer powers can still overpower the rescue despite the speed.","Hex: Under Your Thumb can cap running Haste while the Hex remains lit."],"pros":["Extremely strong endgame numbers.","Global teammate information.","Combines rescue speed, healing speed, and post-unhook mobility."],"cons":["Dead for the majority of every Trial.","Requires the team to reach powered gates.","Cannot help the team get to endgame."],"analysis":["No One Left Behind takes this position because its endgame package is extraordinary. Once the gates are powered, healing and unhooking can be twice as fast at Tier III, every teammate becomes visible, and an unhooked Survivor receives 20% Haste for fifteen seconds.","Those effects are exactly what an endgame rescue needs. Faster interaction reduces the window for interruption, the Aura layer tells you where everyone is positioned, and the Haste can carry the rescued player out of a collapsing hook area.","The ranking penalty is entirely activation timing. The perk contributes zero value to the first five generators, which means it cannot help repair a losing match into a winning one. That is the same structural issue that holds Hope back, only more severe because No One Left Behind is primarily rescue-focused.","If your build is intentionally designed around endgame heroics, the perk can perform far above this position. As a blind general slot, however, we cannot ignore how long it stays completely dormant."],"verdict":"A spectacular endgame rescue perk with a brutal opportunity cost: it does nothing until the gates are powered. When active, its numbers are genuinely excellent.","publicationStatus":"published","reviewFlags":["10.2-live-change","v15-schema-migrated","rank-review-applied","queue-rating:audit-explicit"],"tags":[],"queueRatingStatus":"reviewed","rankRange":[80,100],"rankConfidence":"Low","rankStatus":"stable","evidenceStatus":"strong-inference","acquisition":{"type":"general","sourceCharacter":"General"},"synergyPerkIds":["hope","babysitter","borrowed-time","kindred"],"synergyOther":[],"antiSynergyPerkIds":[],"archetypeRatings":[],"synergies":["Hope","Babysitter","Borrowed Time","Kindred"],"antiSynergies":[],"name":"No One Left Behind","alternateName":null,"source":"General perk","status":"Live 10.2.0","currentEffect":"When all Generators are completed, you see the Auras of other Survivors and heal and unhook other Survivors 80/90/100% faster. Whenever you unhook a Survivor, they gain 10% more Haste.","activation":["All Generators must be completed.","Ends/deactivates when: The effects are inactive until all Generators are completed; once activated, they last through the remainder of the Trial."],"patchNote":"Latest live balance change (10.2.0): Raised the healing-other-Survivors and unhook speed bonuses from 50/75/100% to 80/90/100%; existing Aura and post-unhook Haste enhancement remain.","plainEnglishSummary":"After the Generators are finished, you see teammates, heal and unhook them much faster, and increase the Haste of Survivors you unhook.","cooldown":null,"duration":["Aura reading and action-speed effects: from all Generators completed until the Trial ends.","The additional Haste applies to the rescued Survivor's post-unhook Haste effect."],"tokenOrStackBehavior":null,"oncePerTrialOrOtherLimits":null,"statusEffectsInvolved":["Haste"],"specialInteractions":["The unhook effect increases the rescued Survivor's existing post-unhook Haste by 10%; the patch notes express this as '10% more Haste' rather than a standalone total."],"sourceCharacter":"General","isGeneralPerk":true,"currentLivePatchVerified":"10.2.0"},{"id":"fogwise","rank":89,"tier":"B","roles":["Information","Objective"],"summary":"While repairing, each Great Skill Check reveals the Killer's Aura for several seconds.","metaStatus":"Good","skillLevel":"High","soloQ":3,"swf":3,"unlockPriority":"High","glossaryKeys":["aura-reading","pressure"],"useCases":["Track the Killer while remaining productive on a generator.","Use repeated Great Skill Checks to decide whether to stay, hide, or rotate.","Pair with Skill Check support for more reliable Aura reads."],"counters":["Requires Great Skill Checks.","Undetectable or Aura-blocking effects can deny reads.","No value while you are away from generators."],"pros":["Turns objective skill into Killer information.","Can trigger repeatedly.","Excellent synergy with Great Skill Check builds."],"cons":["Skill-dependent.","Generator-only trigger.","Information can be redundant if the Killer is already visible."],"analysis":["Fogwise rewards accurate Great basic Skill Checks during Generator repair with repeated Killer Aura information, letting a productive Survivor decide whether to stay, hide, or rotate without leaving the objective.","The old Stake Out safety-net interaction no longer exists in live 10.2 because Stake Out special checks no longer activate other Skill Check perks. Hyperfocus can still share the same high-skill Generator shell, but it does not make Fogwise easier to trigger.","The main limitation is context. Fogwise does nothing during chase, rescue, or healing, and it is only as consistent as the user's ability to land Great basic Skill Checks.","That keeps it below universal information perks, while preserving a real niche for generator-focused players with strong Skill Check consistency."],"verdict":"A strong generator-information perk for players who can hit Greats consistently. Fogwise keeps you productive while answering the most important question: where is the Killer?","publicationStatus":"published","tags":["Aura Reading"],"queueRatingStatus":"reviewed","rankRange":null,"rankConfidence":"Not assessed","rankStatus":"inherited","evidenceStatus":"inherited","acquisition":{"type":"character","sourceCharacter":"Vittorio Toscano"},"synergyPerkIds":["hyperfocus","eyes-of-belmont","deja-vu"],"synergyOther":[],"antiSynergyPerkIds":["stake-out"],"archetypeRatings":[],"reviewFlags":["v15-schema-migrated","queue-rating:normalized-tier-plus-v14-specialization-signal"],"synergies":["Hyperfocus","Eyes of Belmont","Déjà Vu"],"antiSynergies":["Stake Out"],"name":"Fogwise","alternateName":null,"source":"Vittorio Toscano","status":"Live 10.2.0","currentEffect":"While repairing a Generator, succeeding a Great Skill Check reveals the Killer's Aura to you for 4/5/6 seconds.","activation":["You must be repairing a Generator and succeed a Great Skill Check.","Ends/deactivates when: The Aura reveal ends after the tier's duration."],"patchNote":"Latest live balance change (unknown): No material live balance change could be verified from available patch history.","plainEnglishSummary":"A Great Skill Check while repairing briefly reveals the Killer's Aura to you.","cooldown":null,"duration":["Killer Aura reveal: 4/5/6 seconds (Tier I/II/III)."],"tokenOrStackBehavior":null,"oncePerTrialOrOtherLimits":null,"statusEffectsInvolved":[],"specialInteractions":[],"sourceCharacter":"Vittorio Toscano","isGeneralPerk":false,"currentLivePatchVerified":"10.2.0"},{"id":"saboteur","rank":90,"tier":"B","roles":["Rescue","Information"],"summary":"When the Killer picks up a teammate, reveal nearby Hook Auras including Scourge Hooks and let you sabotage without a Toolbox.","metaStatus":"Good","skillLevel":"High","soloQ":2,"swf":4,"unlockPriority":"High","glossaryKeys":["hook-state","bodyblock","protection-hit"],"useCases":["Identify the Killer's likely hook route before committing to a sabotage.","Remove a key hook to force a longer carry path.","Target yellow Scourge Hooks specifically to deny powerful Scourge Hook perks."],"counters":["The Killer can choose another hook.","Toolboxless sabotage has a cooldown.","Poor timing can result in a free hit without preventing the hook."],"pros":["Strong hook-route information.","Can deny Scourge Hook value.","Does not require bringing a Toolbox."],"cons":["High positioning demand.","Often needs team coordination.","Can cost generator tempo when the save is unrealistic."],"analysis":["Saboteur takes this position because the information portion is almost as important as the sabotage itself. Seeing the nearby hook network, with Scourge Hooks highlighted separately, lets the Survivor immediately judge whether a carry denial is realistic.","A successful sabotage can create a major swing. The Killer may be forced into a distant hook, take extra bodyblocks, or lose the carry entirely. Denying a critical Scourge Hook can also remove perk value beyond the hook state itself.","The danger is hero-play syndrome. Running across the map for every pickup can destroy generator tempo, and many hook layouts simply give the Killer another easy option. Strong Saboteur play depends on recognizing the few carries that are actually vulnerable.","That specialization keeps it in B. In coordinated save builds it performs much higher; in ordinary Solo Q, it is often an information perk with occasional sabotage opportunities."],"verdict":"A strong carry-denial specialist with valuable hook information. Saboteur rewards choosing the right save, not attempting every save.","publicationStatus":"published","tags":["Hook Denial"],"queueRatingStatus":"reviewed","rankRange":null,"rankConfidence":"Not assessed","rankStatus":"inherited","evidenceStatus":"inherited","acquisition":{"type":"character","sourceCharacter":"Jake Park"},"synergyPerkIds":["breakout","background-player","boil-over","empathy"],"synergyOther":[],"antiSynergyPerkIds":[],"archetypeRatings":[],"reviewFlags":["v15-schema-migrated","queue-rating:normalized-tier-plus-v14-specialization-signal"],"synergies":["Breakout","Background Player","Boil Over","Empathy"],"antiSynergies":[],"name":"Saboteur","alternateName":null,"source":"Jake Park","status":"Live 10.2.0","currentEffect":"While the Killer carries another Survivor, reveals the Auras of all Hooks within 56 m of the original pickup location; normal Hooks appear white and Scourge Hooks yellow. Grants the ability to sabotage Hooks without a Toolbox and increases toolboxless sabotage speed by 30%. Using this toolboxless sabotage ability starts the tiered cooldown.","activation":["Hook auras are revealed while the Killer is carrying another Survivor.","The sabotage-speed effect applies to sabotage performed without a Toolbox.","Ends/deactivates when: Hook aura reading ends when the Killer is no longer carrying a Survivor.","Ends/deactivates when: The toolboxless sabotage speed ability is unavailable during its cooldown."],"patchNote":"Latest live balance change (7.1.0): Reduced the cooldown to 70/65/60 seconds and toolboxless sabotage time to 2.3 seconds.","plainEnglishSummary":"Shows nearby hooks while the Killer carries someone and lets you sabotage hooks without a Toolbox, with a cooldown.","cooldown":"70/65/60 seconds after toolboxless sabotage use","duration":["Hook auras are revealed for the duration the Killer carries the Survivor."],"tokenOrStackBehavior":null,"oncePerTrialOrOtherLimits":null,"statusEffectsInvolved":[],"specialInteractions":["Normal Hooks are white and Scourge Hooks are yellow while revealed."],"sourceCharacter":"Jake Park","isGeneralPerk":false,"currentLivePatchVerified":"10.2.0"},{"id":"deception","rank":91,"tier":"B","roles":["Stealth","Chase"],"summary":"Fake a fast Locker entry while running, create a noise notification there, and hide Scratch Marks and Blood for 5 seconds.","metaStatus":"Good","skillLevel":"High","soloQ":3,"swf":3,"unlockPriority":"Medium–High","glossaryKeys":["looping"],"useCases":["Break line of sight near a Locker and sell the fake entry.","Use the 5-second trail suppression to continue past the Locker without leaving the expected path.","Pair repeated 15-second cooldown mindgames with Locker-oriented builds."],"counters":["Experienced Killers can ignore obvious fake Locker attempts.","Direct sight, Aura reading, and sound can reveal the continued route.","The trick is weaker when the map has no useful nearby Locker."],"pros":["Very short cooldown.","Combines false information with trail suppression.","Can create real chase mistakes against a conditioned Killer."],"cons":["Mindgame-dependent.","No direct distance or health-state protection.","Can become predictable if overused."],"analysis":["Deception ranks this position because its modern 15-second cooldown and five-second trail suppression make it more than a comedy perk. The Locker notification presents one story while hidden Scratch Marks and Blood allow the Survivor to tell another.","The perk gets stronger over multiple encounters. Once a Killer has seen you use Deception, they may start second-guessing real Locker entries as well, especially in builds that also contain Head On or Quick & Quiet.","The skill is selling the fake. Triggering Deception in full view accomplishes little. Breaking line of sight first and choosing a Locker positioned near multiple possible routes is what converts the perk into chase value.","It stays in B because it never guarantees a mistake. Strong Killers can keep visual contact or simply refuse to check the Locker. Deception rewards creativity, not certainty."],"verdict":"A genuinely useful misdirection perk in practiced hands. Deception creates false information, but the Survivor still has to make the lie believable.","publicationStatus":"published","tags":["Misdirection"],"queueRatingStatus":"reviewed","rankRange":null,"rankConfidence":"Not assessed","rankStatus":"inherited","evidenceStatus":"inherited","acquisition":{"type":"character","sourceCharacter":"Élodie Rakoto"},"synergyPerkIds":["head-on","quick-quiet","iron-will","parental-guidance"],"synergyOther":[],"antiSynergyPerkIds":[],"archetypeRatings":[],"reviewFlags":["v15-schema-migrated","queue-rating:normalized-tier-plus-v14-specialization-signal"],"synergies":["Head On","Quick & Quiet","Iron Will","Parental Guidance"],"antiSynergies":[],"name":"Deception","alternateName":null,"source":"Élodie Rakoto","status":"Live 10.2.0","currentEffect":"While running, interact with a Locker to fake entering it: you run past instead, the Locker door opens and closes, and a Loud Noise notification is created at that Locker. Your Scratch Marks and Pools of Blood are suppressed for 5 seconds. Cooldown: 25/20/15 seconds.","activation":["Be running near a Locker and use the interaction input.","Ends/deactivates when: Scratch Mark and Pool of Blood suppression ends after 5 seconds."],"patchNote":"Latest live balance change (8.6.0): Reduced the cooldown to 25/20/15 seconds.","plainEnglishSummary":"A fake Locker entry creates a decoy noise while briefly hiding your trail.","cooldown":"25/20/15 seconds by tier","duration":["Scratch Marks and Pools of Blood suppressed for 5 seconds."],"tokenOrStackBehavior":null,"oncePerTrialOrOtherLimits":null,"statusEffectsInvolved":[],"specialInteractions":["The fake Locker interaction creates a Loud Noise notification at the Locker."],"sourceCharacter":"Élodie Rakoto","isGeneralPerk":false,"currentLivePatchVerified":"10.2.0"},{"id":"open-handed","rank":92,"tier":"B","roles":["Information","Team Support"],"summary":"Increase the radius of qualifying Survivor Aura-reading effects by up to 16 metres for the whole team.","metaStatus":"Good","skillLevel":"Low","soloQ":3,"swf":4,"unlockPriority":"Medium–High","glossaryKeys":["aura-reading","swf"],"useCases":["Extend Kindred's local Killer-read radius around a hook.","Increase the reach of Bond and other range-based Survivor Aura effects.","Support an entire team's Aura builds from one perk slot."],"counters":["Does nothing for Aura effects that are not range-based in the supported way.","Only one Open-Handed effect can benefit a Survivor at a time.","Very weak in a build with no compatible Aura perks."],"pros":["Teamwide multiplier.","Sixteen metres is a large range increase.","Exceptional synergy with some already-good information perks."],"cons":["Nearly useless alone.","Requires compatible Aura effects.","Build-dependent rather than self-contained."],"analysis":["Open-Handed takes this position because sixteen extra metres can meaningfully change several Aura perks. Kindred is the famous example: expanding the local Killer-read area around a hook can expose movement that would otherwise fall just outside the normal radius.","The teamwide nature is important. One copy can strengthen compatible Aura reading for every Survivor, allowing coordinated teams to build around the effect without spending four perk slots on it.","The weakness is absolute dependency on synergy. Open-Handed does nothing useful by itself, and not every Aura effect can be extended. A player who equips it without compatible perks has effectively surrendered a slot.","That makes it a strong build multiplier rather than a strong standalone perk. With the right information package it can outperform this rank; without one, it belongs near the bottom of the list."],"verdict":"One of the better pure synergy perks. Open-Handed can supercharge strong Aura builds, but it has essentially no independent floor.","publicationStatus":"published","tags":["Aura Reading","Team","Synergy"],"queueRatingStatus":"reviewed","rankRange":null,"rankConfidence":"Not assessed","rankStatus":"inherited","evidenceStatus":"inherited","acquisition":{"type":"character","sourceCharacter":"Ace Visconti"},"synergyPerkIds":["kindred","bond","detective-s-hunch","still-sight"],"synergyOther":[],"antiSynergyPerkIds":[],"archetypeRatings":[],"reviewFlags":["v15-schema-migrated","queue-rating:normalized-tier-plus-v14-specialization-signal"],"synergies":["Kindred","Bond","Detective's Hunch","Still Sight"],"antiSynergies":[],"name":"Open-Handed","alternateName":null,"source":"Ace Visconti","status":"Live 10.2.0","currentEffect":"All Survivors benefit from a permanent increase of 8/12/16 metres to the radius of Aura-reading abilities. Open-Handed only affects Auras that emanate from the Survivor causing them, and a Survivor can be affected by only one instance of Open-Handed at a time.","activation":["The perk is equipped; the Aura-reading radius modifier is always active.","Ends/deactivates when: The effect ends with the Trial or if the perk is no longer active."],"patchNote":"Latest live balance change (4.7.0): Increased the Aura-reading radius bonus to 8/12/16 metres and made it non-stacking.","plainEnglishSummary":"It increases the range of Aura-reading abilities for all Survivors by the equipped user's tier value.","cooldown":null,"duration":["Permanent for the Trial while equipped."],"tokenOrStackBehavior":null,"oncePerTrialOrOtherLimits":"A Survivor can be affected by only one instance of Open-Handed at a time.","statusEffectsInvolved":[],"specialInteractions":["Only increases range for Aura-reading abilities that emanate from the Survivor causing them; it does not extend Auras generated by other sources.","Multiple Open-Handed copies do not stack on a Survivor."],"sourceCharacter":"Ace Visconti","isGeneralPerk":false,"currentLivePatchVerified":"10.2.0"},{"id":"second-wind","rank":93,"tier":"B","roles":["Healing","Anti-Tunnel","Self-Sustain"],"summary":"After healing another Survivor for one full Health State, your next unhook starts a short Broken timer that automatically heals you if you avoid going down.","metaStatus":"Good","skillLevel":"Low–Medium","soloQ":3,"swf":3,"unlockPriority":"Medium–High","glossaryKeys":["health-state","broken","anti-tunnel","tunneling"],"useCases":["Bank a future post-unhook heal through normal altruistic play.","Force a tunneling Killer to down you before the automatic heal finishes.","Skip the need to find a teammate for a post-unhook reset."],"counters":["You must complete a full teammate heal first.","Going down before the timer finishes cancels the heal.","Broken prevents ordinary healing during the countdown."],"pros":["Automatic health-state recovery after unhook.","Rewards useful team healing.","No teammate required for the eventual self-heal."],"cons":["Requires setup before being hooked.","Tunnel pressure can cancel the payoff.","Broken timer can be awkward if a safe heal is already available."],"analysis":["Second Wind ranks this position because its payoff is clean once armed: survive a short period after unhook and receive an automatic health state. That can save a full healing interaction and return the Survivor to Healthy without pulling another teammate off objectives.","The activation cost is reasonable but real. You must first heal another Survivor for the equivalent of one Health State, meaning the perk can fail to arm before your first hook if the match does not present the opportunity.","Against tunneling, the timer creates a small test. If the Killer cannot down you before it expires, you effectively gain another health state mid-chase. If they do down you, the perk provides nothing.","That makes Second Wind a respectable self-sustain perk. Its ceiling is useful and its setup encourages good team play, but the heal arrives on a schedule the Killer can actively interrupt."],"verdict":"A solid banked post-unhook heal. Second Wind rewards altruism with future independence, but tunnel pressure can erase the entire payoff.","publicationStatus":"published","tags":[],"queueRatingStatus":"reviewed","rankRange":null,"rankConfidence":"Not assessed","rankStatus":"inherited","evidenceStatus":"inherited","acquisition":{"type":"character","sourceCharacter":"Steve Harrington"},"synergyPerkIds":["babysitter","off-the-record","resurgence","well-make-it"],"synergyOther":[],"antiSynergyPerkIds":[],"archetypeRatings":[],"reviewFlags":["v15-schema-migrated","queue-rating:normalized-tier-plus-v14-specialization-signal"],"synergies":["Babysitter","Off the Record","Resurgence","We'll Make It"],"antiSynergies":[],"name":"Second Wind","alternateName":null,"source":"Steve Harrington","status":"Live 10.2.0","currentEffect":"Healing another Survivor for the equivalent of 1 Health State activates the perk. The next time you are unhooked or unhook yourself, you become Broken until the perk deactivates and are automatically healed by 1 Health State after 28/24/20 seconds. It deactivates if the heal succeeds or you enter the Dying State before the timer elapses. It cannot activate while you are already Broken.","activation":["Heal another Survivor for the equivalent of 1 Health State.","After activation, be unhooked or unhook yourself.","Ends/deactivates when: The delayed heal succeeds.","Ends/deactivates when: You enter the Dying State before the timer elapses.","Ends/deactivates when: The perk cannot activate if you already have Broken."],"patchNote":"Latest live balance change (4.5.0): Reduced the delayed-heal duration to 28/24/20 seconds.","plainEnglishSummary":"After healing a teammate, your next unhook starts a delayed self-heal, unless you are downed first.","cooldown":null,"duration":["The automatic heal occurs after 28/24/20 seconds."],"tokenOrStackBehavior":null,"oncePerTrialOrOtherLimits":null,"statusEffectsInvolved":["Broken"],"specialInteractions":["Broken is applied after the unhook and remains until the perk deactivates."],"sourceCharacter":"Steve Harrington","isGeneralPerk":false,"currentLivePatchVerified":"10.2.0"},{"id":"potential-energy","rank":94,"tier":"B","roles":["Objective"],"summary":"Store up to 20% worth of repair as Tokens instead of progressing the current generator, then dump those Tokens into another generator later; taking damage loses the stored Tokens.","metaStatus":"Good","skillLevel":"High","soloQ":2,"swf":4,"unlockPriority":"Medium–High","glossaryKeys":["pressure","swf"],"useCases":["Move progress from a safe generator into a dangerous central or 3-gen-breaking objective.","Bank objective value before rotating to a generator the Killer is heavily defending.","Coordinate a sudden burst completion in SWF."],"counters":["Taking damage deletes all stored Tokens.","While storing, the current generator is not advancing normally.","Poor macro decisions can simply move progress around without creating a net advantage."],"pros":["Unique ability to transfer repair effort between generators.","Useful against difficult generator layouts.","Can create burst objective pressure."],"cons":["Risk of losing all stored value.","High macro requirement.","No inherent speed increase."],"analysis":["Potential Energy earns this position because its value is strategic rather than numerical. The perk does not create free repair speed; it lets the Survivor decide where their repair investment eventually lands.","That becomes useful against dangerous generator clusters. A Survivor can work safely elsewhere, store Tokens, then rotate into the contested generator and inject progress before the Killer has time to fully respond.","The entire mechanic is punished by taking damage. Losing twenty stored Tokens can erase a large chunk of personal tempo, so the user must understand Killer position and choose the transfer window carefully.","SWF can exploit Potential Energy much better because the team can coordinate when a burst completion matters. In ordinary Solo Q it is easier to overcomplicate a situation that simple generator repair would have solved."],"verdict":"A clever anti-3-gen and burst-progress tool, not a repair-speed perk. Potential Energy rewards macro planning and punishes greed brutally.","publicationStatus":"published","tags":["Progress Transfer","Macro"],"queueRatingStatus":"reviewed","rankRange":null,"rankConfidence":"Not assessed","rankStatus":"inherited","evidenceStatus":"inherited","acquisition":{"type":"character","sourceCharacter":"Vittorio Toscano"},"synergyPerkIds":["deja-vu","prove-thyself","hyperfocus","sprint-burst"],"synergyOther":[],"antiSynergyPerkIds":[],"archetypeRatings":[],"reviewFlags":["v15-schema-migrated","queue-rating:normalized-tier-plus-v14-specialization-signal"],"synergies":["Déjà Vu","Prove Thyself","Hyperfocus","Sprint Burst"],"antiSynergies":[],"name":"Potential Energy","alternateName":null,"source":"Vittorio Toscano","status":"Live 10.2.0","currentEffect":"While repairing a Generator, press Active Ability to store Potential Energy: repair charges no longer progress that Generator and instead yield 1 Token per equivalent 1% progression, up to 10/15/20. A failed Repair Skill Check below the token cap removes 20% of accumulated Tokens; a failed check at the cap regresses the Generator by 10%. With at least one Token, press Active Ability again on the same or another Generator to spend all Tokens and instantly progress that Generator by 1% per Token. The perk deactivates after use or losing a Health State; losing a Health State also removes all stored Tokens.","activation":["Be repairing a Generator and press Active Ability to store progress as Tokens.","Have at least one Token and press Active Ability on a Generator to spend the stored Tokens.","Ends/deactivates when: Deactivates after spending Tokens.","Ends/deactivates when: Losing any Health State deactivates the perk and removes all accumulated Tokens."],"patchNote":"Latest live balance change (9.1.0): Removed the minimum repair time to activate, changed the conversion to 1% repair progress per Token, and set the cap to 10/15/20 Tokens by tier.","plainEnglishSummary":"It converts Generator repair into capped tokens that can be spent as instant progress on another Generator, but is lost after use or taking damage.","cooldown":null,"duration":[],"tokenOrStackBehavior":"Gain 1 Token per 1% equivalent repair progression, up to 10/15/20. Below the cap, a failed Repair Skill Check removes 20% of accumulated Tokens; at the cap, a failed check regresses the Generator by 10% instead. Spending Tokens consumes all of them, each yielding 1% instant Generator progression. Losing a Health State removes all Tokens.","oncePerTrialOrOtherLimits":"The perk deactivates after use or losing any Health State, so it cannot be used again in that Trial after either event.","statusEffectsInvolved":[],"specialInteractions":["Token charge rate is affected by repair-speed effects and Generator repair progression bonuses, including Great Skill Check bonus progression."],"sourceCharacter":"Vittorio Toscano","isGeneralPerk":false,"currentLivePatchVerified":"10.2.0"},{"id":"specialist","rank":95,"tier":"B","roles":["Objective","Item"],"summary":"Chest interactions grant Tokens that can be cashed on a Great generator Skill Check to permanently reduce that generator's required repair charges.","metaStatus":"Good","skillLevel":"High","soloQ":3,"swf":4,"unlockPriority":"Medium","glossaryKeys":["pressure"],"useCases":["Convert chest time into permanent generator requirement reduction.","Use several Tokens at once on a difficult generator that the Killer keeps regressing.","Pair chest builds with objective pressure rather than treating looting as pure side activity."],"counters":["Requires unlocking or rummaging through Chests.","Needs a Great Skill Check to cash Tokens.","Chest-search time can outweigh the generator value if done inefficiently."],"pros":["Permanent objective reduction is difficult for the Killer to undo.","Can bank multiple Tokens.","Adds objective purpose to chest builds."],"cons":["Heavy setup.","Chest availability is finite.","Great Skill Check requirement adds another failure point."],"analysis":["Specialist sits at this position because permanent repair-charge reduction is a meaningful reward attached to a costly economy. Each chest interaction can create Tokens, and a later Great Skill Check converts those Tokens into progress the Killer cannot simply regress away in the usual manner.","The perk is strongest when chest interactions already serve another purpose. Appraisal, Plunderer's Instinct, or a resource-focused build can make the setup less wasteful because the player receives items and Specialist Tokens from the same activity.","The danger is opportunity cost. Opening several chests to create objective progress can be slower than repairing a generator directly, especially if the chests are far apart or yield little item value.","That makes Specialist a niche but respectable objective perk. It can produce surprising permanent progress, but it asks the Survivor to build and route around it."],"verdict":"A permanent-progress perk with a chest tax. Specialist is strongest when looting is already part of the plan, not when you detour across the map just to manufacture Tokens.","publicationStatus":"published","tags":["Chest","Permanent Progress"],"queueRatingStatus":"reviewed","rankRange":null,"rankConfidence":"Not assessed","rankStatus":"inherited","evidenceStatus":"inherited","acquisition":{"type":"character","sourceCharacter":"Lara Croft"},"synergyPerkIds":["appraisal","plunderers-instinct","fogwise"],"synergyOther":[],"antiSynergyPerkIds":["stake-out"],"archetypeRatings":[],"reviewFlags":["v15-schema-migrated","queue-rating:normalized-tier-plus-v14-specialization-signal"],"synergies":["Appraisal","Plunderer's Instinct","Fogwise"],"antiSynergies":["Stake Out"],"name":"Specialist","alternateName":null,"source":"Lara Croft","status":"Live 10.2.0","currentEffect":"Unlocking or rummaging through a Chest grants 1 Token, up to 6. A successful Great Repair Skill Check while repairing a Generator consumes all tokens and permanently reduces that Generator's required Repair Charges by 2/3/4 per token, up to 12/18/24 charges.","activation":["Unlock or rummage through a Chest to gain tokens.","Hit a Great Repair Skill Check while repairing a Generator to spend them.","Ends/deactivates when: Tokens are consumed when a Great Repair Skill Check triggers the effect."],"patchNote":"Latest live balance change (8.1.0): Introduced; no later material live balance change located in the official notes checked.","plainEnglishSummary":"Chest interactions bank tokens that a Great repair check spends to permanently reduce that Generator's repair requirement.","cooldown":null,"duration":["The Generator charge reduction is permanent for that Generator for the Trial."],"tokenOrStackBehavior":"Gain 1 token per Chest unlocked or rummaged, capped at 6. A qualifying Great Repair Skill Check consumes all tokens.","oncePerTrialOrOtherLimits":null,"statusEffectsInvolved":[],"specialInteractions":["The consumed tokens reduce the charge requirement of the Generator being repaired when the Great check succeeds."],"sourceCharacter":"Lara Croft","isGeneralPerk":false,"currentLivePatchVerified":"10.2.0"},{"id":"exultation","rank":96,"tier":"B","roles":["Item","Pallet","Objective"],"summary":"A pallet stun upgrades your held Item by one rarity and, when upgraded, restores a large portion of its Charges.","metaStatus":"Good","skillLevel":"High","soloQ":3,"swf":4,"unlockPriority":"Medium","glossaryKeys":["looping"],"useCases":["Upgrade a weaker Toolbox, Med-Kit, or Flashlight while simultaneously recharging it.","Turn successful pallet stuns into long-term resource value.","Pair with item-centered builds where extra Charges matter throughout the Trial."],"counters":["Requires landing a pallet stun.","An already maximum-rarity Item cannot be upgraded and therefore does not receive the recharge.","You must still bring or find an Item worth improving."],"pros":["Seventy-five percent recharge is substantial.","Can improve both rarity and remaining resource pool.","Short cooldown if repeated stuns are available."],"cons":["Trigger is Killer-interaction dependent.","No value with a max-rarity Item.","Requires item planning."],"analysis":["Exultation ranks this position because its modern 75% recharge can be a serious resource swing. A successful pallet stun can both upgrade the Item and return most of its charges, creating far more value than the perk's original version.","The best targets are Items whose additional charges translate directly into time or survival, such as Toolboxes and Med-Kits. The pallet stun becomes more than a chase win; it becomes a resource refresh that continues paying afterward.","The restriction around maximum rarity matters. Once the Item can no longer upgrade, the recharge component stops being available through the same interaction, limiting repeated use with already-premium gear.","Exultation is therefore a strong build-around perk rather than general utility. Players who plan around an upgradeable Item and land stuns can extract impressive value; everyone else should choose something more reliable."],"verdict":"A strong item-economy reward for successful pallet play. Exultation can generate huge resource value, but only if your Item still has somewhere to upgrade.","publicationStatus":"published","tags":["Resource"],"queueRatingStatus":"reviewed","rankRange":null,"rankConfidence":"Not assessed","rankStatus":"inherited","evidenceStatus":"inherited","acquisition":{"type":"character","sourceCharacter":"Trevor Belmont"},"synergyPerkIds":["built-to-last","any-means-necessary","smash-hit"],"synergyOther":[],"antiSynergyPerkIds":[],"archetypeRatings":[],"reviewFlags":["v15-schema-migrated","queue-rating:normalized-tier-plus-v14-specialization-signal"],"synergies":["Built to Last","Any Means Necessary","Smash Hit"],"antiSynergies":[],"name":"Exultation","alternateName":null,"source":"Trevor Belmont","status":"Live 10.2.0","currentEffect":"While you are holding an Item, stunning the Killer by dropping a Pallet recharges the Item by 75% and upgrades its Rarity to the next available tier. Exultation then has a 30/25/20-second cooldown. An Item already at maximum rarity cannot be upgraded and therefore does not receive this recharge.","activation":["You must be holding an Item.","You must stun the Killer by dropping a Pallet.","Ends/deactivates when: The perk cannot trigger while on cooldown."],"patchNote":"Latest live balance change (9.0.0): Increased Item recharge from 25% to 75% and reduced cooldown from 40/35/30 to 30/25/20 seconds.","plainEnglishSummary":"A Pallet stun while holding an Item improves and recharges it, then puts the perk on cooldown.","cooldown":"30/25/20 seconds (Tier I/II/III), after the trigger.","duration":[],"tokenOrStackBehavior":null,"oncePerTrialOrOtherLimits":null,"statusEffectsInvolved":[],"specialInteractions":["An Item at maximum Rarity cannot advance to the next tier, so the recharge effect does not occur for that trigger."],"sourceCharacter":"Trevor Belmont","isGeneralPerk":false,"currentLivePatchVerified":"10.2.0"},{"id":"solidarity","rank":97,"tier":"B","roles":["Healing","Objective","Self-Sustain"],"summary":"While injured, convert up to 75% of the healing you give another Survivor into progress on your own heal, including when using a Med-Kit.","metaStatus":"Good","skillLevel":"Low–Medium","soloQ":4,"swf":3,"unlockPriority":"High","glossaryKeys":["reset","health-state"],"useCases":["Turn one teammate heal into substantial progress on your own health bar.","Combine two injured Survivors' reset needs into less total healing time.","Pair with strong altruistic healing bonuses so the shared reset becomes even faster."],"counters":["You must already be injured and heal another Survivor .","It never completes your own heal unless enough progress is generated or someone finishes it afterward.","If the team should remain injured and repair, healing at all can still be the wrong macro choice."],"pros":["Excellent two-for-one healing efficiency.","70% conversion is substantial.","Requires no token, cooldown, or special map object."],"cons":["Needs another injured Survivor to heal.","Does not help when you are the one receiving the heal first.","Still tied to the strategic value of healing in that match."],"analysis":["Solidarity became cleaner in 10.2. The conversion rate now reaches 75% and the old restriction against using a Med-Kit on the other Survivor is gone.","The perk still shines when two Survivors need a reset. One altruistic heal advances both health bars, reducing the total team time needed before both players can return to objectives.","Allowing Med-Kits broadens the build space because the user can accelerate the teammate heal with an Item without disabling Solidarity’s personal progress.","The buff is incremental rather than transformational, but it raises an already-efficient support perk and deserves consideration above its previous placement."],"verdict":"A better two-for-one heal in 10.2: 75% conversion and no Med-Kit restriction make Solidarity easier to exploit without changing its core job.","publicationStatus":"published","reviewFlags":["10.2-live-change","v15-schema-migrated","queue-rating:normalized-tier-plus-v14-specialization-signal"],"tags":["Efficiency"],"queueRatingStatus":"reviewed","rankRange":null,"rankConfidence":"Not assessed","rankStatus":"inherited","evidenceStatus":"inherited","acquisition":{"type":"character","sourceCharacter":"Jane Romero"},"synergyPerkIds":["botany-knowledge","well-make-it","desperate-measures","empathy"],"synergyOther":[],"antiSynergyPerkIds":[],"archetypeRatings":[],"synergies":["Botany Knowledge","We'll Make It","Desperate Measures","Empathy"],"antiSynergies":[],"name":"Solidarity","alternateName":null,"source":"Jane Romero","status":"Live 10.2.0","currentEffect":"While injured and healing another Survivor, you also gain healing progress at 65/70/75% speed.","activation":["Be injured and heal another Survivor.","Ends/deactivates when: The self-healing progress effect ends when you stop healing another Survivor or are no longer injured."],"patchNote":"Latest live balance change (10.2.0): Increased parallel self-healing progress from 50/60/70% to 65/70/75% and removed the no-Med-Kit restriction.","plainEnglishSummary":"While injured and healing a teammate, you also build your own healing progress at a reduced rate.","cooldown":null,"duration":[],"tokenOrStackBehavior":null,"oncePerTrialOrOtherLimits":null,"statusEffectsInvolved":[],"specialInteractions":["The 10.2.0 live effect no longer requires healing without a Med-Kit."],"sourceCharacter":"Jane Romero","isGeneralPerk":false,"currentLivePatchVerified":"10.2.0"},{"id":"moment-of-glory","rank":98,"tier":"B","roles":["Self-Sustain","Item","Healing"],"summary":"After one chest interaction, your next injury starts a delayed automatic heal if you avoid being downed for the full timer.","metaStatus":"Good","skillLevel":"Low–Medium","soloQ":3,"swf":3,"unlockPriority":"Medium","glossaryKeys":["broken","health-state"],"useCases":["Pre-arm a future autonomous heal with a single chest.","Use strong chase pathing to survive the delay and recover without teammate help.","Pair chest builds with another form of self-sustain."],"counters":["Requires a chest interaction first.","The heal takes a long time to arrive.","Entering the Dying State cancels the effect."],"pros":["Only one chest is needed in the current version.","Future heal requires no teammate once armed.","Simple activation after setup."],"cons":["Sixty-second Tier III delay is long.","Broken prevents ordinary healing during the countdown.","One down cancels the payoff."],"analysis":["Moment of Glory takes this position because the 10.1 reduction to one chest makes the setup much more reasonable. Once armed, the perk can eventually return an injured Survivor to Healthy without requiring another player or Med-Kit.","The problem is survival time. Sixty seconds is an eternity if the Killer remains on you, and the automatic heal disappears entirely if you enter the Dying State before the timer completes.","That means Moment of Glory performs best for players who can take a hit, break chase, and remain productive while the delayed heal ticks. It is much worse as an anti-tunnel tool because tunnel pressure is precisely what cancels it.","The perk is usable and improved, but still more cumbersome than stronger self-sustain options. One chest is fair setup; a full minute of delayed vulnerability is still a significant cost."],"verdict":"Much better after its one-chest buff, but still slow. Moment of Glory rewards surviving after injury rather than helping you survive the chase that follows it.","publicationStatus":"published","tags":["Chest","Delayed Heal"],"queueRatingStatus":"reviewed","rankRange":null,"rankConfidence":"Not assessed","rankStatus":"inherited","evidenceStatus":"inherited","acquisition":{"type":"character","sourceCharacter":"Trevor Belmont"},"synergyPerkIds":["plunderers-instinct","appraisal","resilience","lithe"],"synergyOther":[],"antiSynergyPerkIds":[],"archetypeRatings":[],"reviewFlags":["v15-schema-migrated","queue-rating:normalized-tier-plus-v14-specialization-signal"],"synergies":["Plunderer's Instinct","Appraisal","Resilience","Lithe"],"antiSynergies":[],"name":"Moment of Glory","alternateName":null,"source":"Trevor Belmont","status":"Live 10.2.0","currentEffect":"After completing an Unlocking or Rummaging action on a Chest once, the perk activates. If you are not already Broken, the next time you become Injured you immediately suffer Broken. If you do not enter the Dying State, you automatically heal one Health State after 80/70/60 seconds. The automatic-heal effect is cancelled early if you enter the Dying State. It does not activate if you already have Broken and deactivates after healing you.","activation":["Complete one Chest Unlocking or Rummaging action.","Not already suffer from Broken when the perk would activate.","Become Injured to start the delayed automatic heal.","Ends/deactivates when: The delayed heal is cancelled if you enter the Dying State.","Ends/deactivates when: The perk deactivates after healing you."],"patchNote":"Latest live balance change (10.1.0): Reduced Chest Unlocking/Rummaging actions required to activate from two to one.","plainEnglishSummary":"After one chest interaction, becoming injured while not Broken makes you Broken and schedules a delayed self-heal unless you are downed first.","cooldown":null,"duration":["Automatic heal delay: 80/70/60 seconds after becoming Injured."],"tokenOrStackBehavior":null,"oncePerTrialOrOtherLimits":"Deactivates after its automatic heal; the current effect description does not separately state a per-Trial use count.","statusEffectsInvolved":["Broken"],"specialInteractions":[],"sourceCharacter":"Trevor Belmont","isGeneralPerk":false,"currentLivePatchVerified":"10.2.0"},{"id":"power-struggle","rank":99,"tier":"B","roles":["Chase","Pallet","Endgame"],"summary":"Once your wiggle progress reaches the threshold while being carried, you can drop a nearby upright Pallet yourself and stun the Killer into releasing you.","metaStatus":"Good","skillLevel":"High","soloQ":2,"swf":4,"unlockPriority":"Medium","glossaryKeys":["dying-state","looping"],"useCases":["Create a self-save when the Killer carries you through an upright pallet.","Pair with Flip-Flop so ground recovery preloads the wiggle threshold.","Use pallet Aura information while downed to position for a possible escape."],"counters":["Requires the Killer to carry you through a usable upright Pallet.","Threshold must be reached before passing the pallet.","After use, the perk deactivates."],"pros":["Can directly free you from the Killer's grasp.","Excellent build synergy.","Pallet Aura information helps setup."],"cons":["Extremely geometry-dependent.","Often needs another perk to become reliable.","One-use payoff."],"analysis":["Power Struggle ranks this position because escaping the Killer's grasp is one of the biggest individual swings available from a perk, but the setup is demanding. You need sufficient wiggle progress and an upright pallet exactly where the carry path passes.","Flip-Flop is the classic partner because ground recovery can pre-convert into wiggle progress, allowing Power Struggle to activate much earlier after pickup. Tenacity and Unbreakable help create the same recovery-oriented shell.","Without that support, the Killer will often reach a hook before the threshold or simply avoid carrying through obvious pallets. Experienced Killers recognize the setup and can path around it.","The ceiling is excellent and the floor is very low. Power Struggle belongs in B as a build-defining anti-carry option, not a perk you can blindly equip for consistent value."],"verdict":"A spectacular self-save perk trapped behind geometry and setup. Power Struggle is excellent in its dedicated build and unreliable everywhere else.","publicationStatus":"published","tags":["Anti-Carry","Escape"],"queueRatingStatus":"reviewed","rankRange":null,"rankConfidence":"Not assessed","rankStatus":"inherited","evidenceStatus":"inherited","acquisition":{"type":"character","sourceCharacter":"Élodie Rakoto"},"synergyPerkIds":["flip-flop","unbreakable","tenacity","boil-over"],"synergyOther":[],"antiSynergyPerkIds":[],"archetypeRatings":[{"archetype":"Flip-Flop pallet-save package","grade":"A-/B+","requires":["flip-flop"],"note":"The combination creates a much higher coordinated ceiling than Power Struggle has as a generic standalone perk.","confidence":"Medium"}],"reviewFlags":["v15-schema-migrated","queue-rating:audit-explicit"],"synergies":["Flip-Flop","Unbreakable","Tenacity","Boil Over"],"antiSynergies":[],"name":"Power Struggle","alternateName":null,"source":"Élodie Rakoto","status":"Live 10.2.0","currentEffect":"While in the Dying State, reveals the Auras of upright Pallets. Once you reach 25/20/15% Wiggle progression while being carried by the Killer, you can drop a nearby Pallet; it stuns the Killer and makes them release you. The perk deactivates after use.","activation":["Be in the Dying State to see upright Pallet Auras.","While being carried, reach the tier-specific Wiggle progression threshold and have a nearby upright Pallet.","Ends/deactivates when: Deactivates after dropping a Pallet with the perk."],"patchNote":"Latest live balance change (5.5.0): Lowered the Wiggle threshold from 35/30/25% to 25/20/15% and added Aura reading for upright Pallets while in the Dying State.","plainEnglishSummary":"While downed and carried, it shows upright Pallets and lets you drop one to stun the Killer after enough wiggle progress.","cooldown":null,"duration":[],"tokenOrStackBehavior":null,"oncePerTrialOrOtherLimits":"Deactivates after use; no separate per-Trial count is stated.","statusEffectsInvolved":[],"specialInteractions":["Flip-Flop can convert Recovery progression into Wiggle progression, which can contribute toward the threshold."],"sourceCharacter":"Élodie Rakoto","isGeneralPerk":false,"currentLivePatchVerified":"10.2.0"},{"id":"self-care","rank":100,"tier":"B","roles":["Healing","Self-Sustain","Utility"],"summary":"Unlock self-healing without a Med-Kit at 35% of normal healing speed at Tier III.","metaStatus":"Good","skillLevel":"Low","soloQ":4,"swf":3,"unlockPriority":"Medium","glossaryKeys":["reset","health-state","solo-q"],"useCases":["Recover independently when no teammate or Med-Kit is available.","Finish a partial heal created by Resurgence or Reactive Healing without spending item charges.","Use in emergencies where being Healthy matters more than the very large time cost."],"counters":["Tier III still heals at only 35% of normal speed.","A full heal consumes an enormous amount of objective time.","Anti-heal effects make the already-slow interaction even worse."],"pros":["Complete independence from teammates and Items.","Always available while healable.","Can efficiently finish already-partial healing bars."],"cons":["Extremely slow from zero progress.","One of the easiest perks to misuse strategically.","Can lose matches when used for unnecessary full self-heals."],"analysis":["Self-Care ranks this position because independence has real value, but the current 35% speed is a severe tax. A full heal from zero is so slow that using the perk automatically after every injury can donate enormous generator tempo to the Killer.","The perk becomes much better when it is finishing partial progress. Resurgence, Reactive Healing, or an interrupted teammate heal can leave only a small portion remaining, and Self-Care lets you complete that remainder without searching for assistance.","Its popularity should not be confused with efficiency. The perk feels safe because it always offers an action, but Dead by Daylight often rewards staying injured and repairing instead of spending a long time restoring a Health State that may be lost again immediately.","That strategic trap keeps Self-Care low B. It is not useless, and in certain independent builds it is genuinely practical, but disciplined use matters more than the perk's mere availability."],"verdict":"Independence at a painful price. Self-Care is best for finishing partial heals or true emergencies, not for disappearing into a corner after every hit.","publicationStatus":"published","tags":["Independence"],"queueRatingStatus":"reviewed","rankRange":[92,115],"rankConfidence":"Medium","rankStatus":"stable","evidenceStatus":"inherited","acquisition":{"type":"character","sourceCharacter":"Claudette Morel"},"synergyPerkIds":["botany-knowledge","desperate-measures","resurgence","reactive-healing"],"synergyOther":[],"antiSynergyPerkIds":[],"archetypeRatings":[],"reviewFlags":["v15-schema-migrated","rank-review-applied","queue-rating:audit-partial-plus-normalized"],"synergies":["Botany Knowledge","Desperate Measures","Resurgence","Reactive Healing"],"antiSynergies":[],"name":"Self-Care","alternateName":null,"source":"Claudette Morel","status":"Live 10.2.0","currentEffect":"Unlocks the ability to self-heal without a Med-Kit at 25/30/35% of the regular Healing speed.","activation":["Be in a state that can be healed and use the self-heal ability.","Ends/deactivates when: Healing ends when interrupted or when the heal is complete."],"patchNote":"Latest live balance change (6.1.0): Reduced self-healing speed to 25/30/35% and removed the Med-Kit efficiency bonus.","plainEnglishSummary":"Lets you heal yourself without a Med-Kit, but at a reduced rate.","cooldown":null,"duration":[],"tokenOrStackBehavior":null,"oncePerTrialOrOtherLimits":null,"statusEffectsInvolved":[],"specialInteractions":["The perk's self-heal does not require a Med-Kit."],"sourceCharacter":"Claudette Morel","isGeneralPerk":false,"currentLivePatchVerified":"10.2.0"},{"id":"flip-flop","rank":101,"tier":"B","roles":["Chase","Recovery","Utility"],"summary":"While downed, convert half of your recovery progress into stored wiggle progress for the moment the Killer picks you up.","metaStatus":"Good","skillLevel":"Low–Medium","soloQ":2,"swf":4,"unlockPriority":"Medium","glossaryKeys":["dying-state"],"useCases":["Preload wiggle progress while the Killer leaves you on the ground.","Enable fast Power Struggle activation after pickup.","Make prolonged slugging increase the risk of a carry escape."],"counters":["Provides little value if the Killer picks you up immediately.","Cannot by itself force the Killer to cross a pallet or miss a hook.","Maximum converted progress is capped."],"pros":["Excellent synergy with anti-carry builds.","Punishes delayed pickups.","Passive while recovering."],"cons":["Very weak standalone.","Requires slug time.","Usually needs another perk to cash the stored progress into something meaningful."],"analysis":["Flip-Flop follows Power Struggle at this position because the two are almost a package. Ground recovery becomes future wiggle progress, which can move Power Struggle past its activation threshold almost immediately after pickup.","Even without Power Struggle, the stored progress makes long slugging more dangerous for the Killer. A Survivor who is left down for a substantial time begins the carry much closer to escaping.","The limitation is that the Killer can deny most of the perk simply by picking up quickly. Flip-Flop also does not control hook distance, carry route, or pallet geometry.","It therefore ranks as a strong synergy piece rather than independent power. In a dedicated recovery build it is foundational; in a general loadout it is difficult to justify."],"verdict":"The engine behind several anti-carry builds. Flip-Flop turns slug time into wiggle pressure, but usually needs another perk or favorable geometry to convert that pressure into an escape.","publicationStatus":"published","tags":["Anti-Carry","Build Synergy"],"queueRatingStatus":"reviewed","rankRange":null,"rankConfidence":"Not assessed","rankStatus":"inherited","evidenceStatus":"inherited","acquisition":{"type":"character","sourceCharacter":"Ash Williams"},"synergyPerkIds":["power-struggle","unbreakable","tenacity","boil-over"],"synergyOther":[],"antiSynergyPerkIds":[],"archetypeRatings":[],"reviewFlags":["v15-schema-migrated","queue-rating:normalized-tier-plus-v14-specialization-signal"],"synergies":["Power Struggle","Unbreakable","Tenacity","Boil Over"],"antiSynergies":[],"name":"Flip-Flop","alternateName":null,"source":"Ash Williams","status":"Live 10.2.0","currentEffect":"While in the Dying State, your Recovery progress also charges your Wiggle Meter at 50% of the Recovery rate, up to a cap of 40/45/50% Wiggle progression. The accumulated Wiggle progress remains available if the Killer picks you up.","activation":["You must be in the Dying State and perform the Recovery action.","Ends/deactivates when: Additional conversion stops at the tier's maximum Wiggle progression cap."],"patchNote":"Latest live balance change (unknown): No material live balance change could be verified from available patch history.","plainEnglishSummary":"Recovering while downed banks part of your Wiggle progress before the Killer picks you up.","cooldown":null,"duration":[],"tokenOrStackBehavior":"Recovery progress is converted to Wiggle progress at 50% of the Recovery rate until the tier-specific cap of 40/45/50% is reached; no tokens are used.","oncePerTrialOrOtherLimits":null,"statusEffectsInvolved":[],"specialInteractions":["The Wiggle progression accumulated while recovering remains when the Survivor is picked up."],"sourceCharacter":"Ash Williams","isGeneralPerk":false,"currentLivePatchVerified":"10.2.0"},{"id":"boil-over","rank":102,"tier":"B","roles":["Chase","Utility"],"summary":"While carried, strengthen wiggle effects, hide nearby Hook Auras from the Killer, and gain a chunk of current wiggle progress if the Killer falls from sufficient height.","metaStatus":"Good","skillLevel":"Low–Medium","soloQ":3,"swf":4,"unlockPriority":"Medium","glossaryKeys":["dying-state"],"useCases":["Make tight indoor or elevated carry routes harder to navigate.","Exploit drops where the Killer must descend while carrying you.","Combine with anti-carry teammates and hook denial."],"counters":["Flat open maps may provide almost no meaningful terrain interaction.","Strong Killers can compensate for stronger wiggle movement.","Nearby hook availability can make the hidden Aura effect irrelevant."],"pros":["Can be oppressive on specific maps and elevated zones.","Requires no active input after downing.","Synergizes naturally with carry-denial builds."],"cons":["Highly map-dependent.","Often accomplishes nothing against short carry routes.","Can encourage unproductive attempts to die in awkward corners."],"analysis":["Boil Over ranks this position because map geometry determines almost everything. On elevated structures and cramped indoor routes, stronger wiggle movement plus hidden nearby Hook Auras can make carrying genuinely uncomfortable.","The drop bonus is where the perk can become dangerous. If the Killer must fall far enough while carrying you, the extra wiggle progress can suddenly turn an ordinary route into an escape threat.","On many maps, none of that happens. The Killer sees a nearby hook, walks ten metres, and hooks normally. Skilled Killers also learn the hook layouts well enough that missing a nearby Aura is not always meaningful.","Boil Over is therefore a classic map-dependent carry-denial perk. Its notorious matches are real, but they are not representative enough to justify a high general ranking."],"verdict":"Annoying and occasionally oppressive on the right terrain, ordinary everywhere else. Boil Over is a map specialist, not a universal anti-carry solution.","publicationStatus":"published","tags":["Anti-Carry","Wiggle","Map Dependent"],"queueRatingStatus":"reviewed","rankRange":null,"rankConfidence":"Not assessed","rankStatus":"inherited","evidenceStatus":"inherited","acquisition":{"type":"character","sourceCharacter":"Kate Denson"},"synergyPerkIds":["flip-flop","breakout","saboteur","power-struggle"],"synergyOther":[],"antiSynergyPerkIds":[],"archetypeRatings":[],"reviewFlags":["v15-schema-migrated","queue-rating:normalized-tier-plus-v14-specialization-signal"],"synergies":["Flip-Flop","Breakout","Saboteur","Power Struggle"],"antiSynergies":[],"name":"Boil Over","alternateName":null,"source":"Kate Denson","status":"Live 10.2.0","currentEffect":"While carried, your wiggle effects are 60/70/80% more effective and the Killer cannot read Hook Auras within 16 metres. If the Killer falls from a height while carrying you, gain 33% of your current wiggle progress.","activation":["Be carried by the Killer.","Killer must fall from a height while carrying you for the extra progress.","Ends/deactivates when: Effects end when the Killer stops carrying you."],"patchNote":"Latest live balance change (5.7.0): Set struggle-effect strength to 60/70/80% (was 50/75/100%).","plainEnglishSummary":"While carried, you wiggle more effectively, hide nearby Hook Auras, and gain progress if the Killer falls.","cooldown":null,"duration":[],"tokenOrStackBehavior":null,"oncePerTrialOrOtherLimits":null,"statusEffectsInvolved":[],"specialInteractions":["The 33% bonus is based on current wiggle progress."],"sourceCharacter":"Kate Denson","isGeneralPerk":false,"currentLivePatchVerified":"10.2.0"},{"id":"buckle-up","rank":103,"tier":"B","roles":["Anti-Slug","Recovery","Mobility"],"summary":"While healing a downed teammate, both of you can see the Killer; completing the pickup gives the rescued Survivor a strong Haste burst and hides their Scratch Marks.","metaStatus":"Good","skillLevel":"Low–Medium","soloQ":3,"swf":3,"unlockPriority":"Medium","glossaryKeys":["dying-state","aura-reading","haste","anti-slug"],"useCases":["Read whether the Killer is returning while you attempt a ground pickup.","Give the recovered teammate enough Haste to escape the immediate area.","Use Scratch-Mark suppression to make the revived Survivor's exit route harder to follow."],"counters":["Only helps during Dying-State heals.","The speed and stealth benefits go to the recovered Survivor, not the healer.","If the Killer hooks promptly, the perk never matters."],"pros":["Built-in Killer information during the risky heal.","Strong escape burst for the recovered teammate.","Easy to understand."],"cons":["Slugging-dependent.","No protection for the healer.","Less powerful than older versions players may remember."],"analysis":["Buckle Up takes this position because the current version still has useful anti-slug value even though it no longer carries the infamous protection package of older metas. The Killer Aura during the heal tells both players whether finishing the pickup is safe.","Once the teammate reaches Injured, their Haste burst can create substantial immediate distance, while hidden Scratch Marks make the path harder to track after line of sight breaks.","The perk's weakness is opportunity. A Killer who hooks downed Survivors normally gives Buckle Up almost nothing to do. Even during slugging, the healer remains vulnerable to interruption.","That makes it a competent recovery-support perk rather than a meta staple. It works well in anti-slug builds, but does not deserve a slot in every match."],"verdict":"A useful modern anti-slug support perk. Buckle Up helps the recovered Survivor escape, but its old reputation should not inflate the strength of the current version.","publicationStatus":"published","tags":[],"queueRatingStatus":"reviewed","rankRange":null,"rankConfidence":"Not assessed","rankStatus":"inherited","evidenceStatus":"inherited","acquisition":{"type":"character","sourceCharacter":"Ash Williams"},"synergyPerkIds":["were-gonna-live-forever","conviction","soul-guard","empathy"],"synergyOther":[],"antiSynergyPerkIds":[],"archetypeRatings":[],"reviewFlags":["v15-schema-migrated","queue-rating:normalized-tier-plus-v14-specialization-signal"],"synergies":["We're Gonna Live Forever","Conviction","Soul Guard","Empathy"],"antiSynergies":[],"name":"Buckle Up","alternateName":null,"source":"Ash Williams","status":"Live 10.2.0","currentEffect":"While healing a Survivor in the Dying State, you both see the Killer's Aura. When you finish healing them into the Injured State, the healed Survivor leaves no Scratch Marks and gains 50% Haste for 3/4/5 seconds.","activation":["Heal another Survivor from the Dying State to Injured.","Ends/deactivates when: Killer Aura reading applies while the healing interaction is in progress.","Ends/deactivates when: Haste and Scratch Mark suppression end after 3/4/5 seconds."],"patchNote":"Latest live balance change (8.0.0): Reworked the perk to its current Dying-State healing and post-heal Haste effect.","plainEnglishSummary":"Healing a downed teammate reveals the Killer, then gives the rescued teammate a brief Haste burst and hides their Scratch Marks.","cooldown":null,"duration":["Killer Aura reading while healing.","Post-heal Haste and no Scratch Marks: 3/4/5 seconds."],"tokenOrStackBehavior":null,"oncePerTrialOrOtherLimits":null,"statusEffectsInvolved":["Haste"],"specialInteractions":["Both you and the healed Survivor see the Killer's Aura while healing a Survivor in the Dying State."],"sourceCharacter":"Ash Williams","isGeneralPerk":false,"currentLivePatchVerified":"10.2.0"},{"id":"mettle-of-man","rank":104,"tier":"B","roles":["Team Support","Chase"],"summary":"After three Protection Hits, gain a one-time shield against the next attack that would put you into the Dying State while Injured.","metaStatus":"Good","skillLevel":"Very High","soloQ":2,"swf":4,"unlockPriority":"Medium","glossaryKeys":["protection-hit","bodyblock","health-state"],"useCases":["Build toward an extra health-state-style protection through deliberate bodyblocks.","Use coordinated protection hits around hooks and carries.","Create a late-match chase where the Killer must land an additional attack."],"counters":["Three Protection Hits are difficult and dangerous to earn.","Poor bodyblocks can feed the Killer free pressure before the perk activates.","After later healing to full, the perk has a significant Aura-related drawback until it deactivates."],"pros":["Successful activation is extremely powerful.","Rewards coordinated team protection.","Can completely alter a critical late chase."],"cons":["Very high setup cost.","Encourages risky play.","Often fails to activate before the match is decided."],"analysis":["Mettle of Man ranks this position because the reward is enormous and the setup is punishing. Three Protection Hits can eventually buy a shield against a downing attack, essentially creating an additional chase resource that most Killers cannot ignore.","The problem is earning those Protection Hits without donating the match. Running in front of the Killer at bad moments creates injuries and healing debt, and some Killers or powers make clean protection hits difficult to register safely.","SWF improves the perk substantially because the team can coordinate carry escorts and hook-defense bodyblocks. In Solo Q, trying to manufacture three hits can easily become selfish or chaotic.","Mettle of Man is therefore powerful in theory and inconsistent in practice. We rank the actual cost of reaching activation, not just the impressive payoff once it is ready."],"verdict":"A huge reward hidden behind one of the most dangerous setup requirements in the game. Mettle of Man can win a chase after activation, but earning it cleanly is the real challenge.","publicationStatus":"published","tags":["Protection Hit","Extra Health State"],"queueRatingStatus":"reviewed","rankRange":null,"rankConfidence":"Not assessed","rankStatus":"inherited","evidenceStatus":"inherited","acquisition":{"type":"character","sourceCharacter":"Ash Williams"},"synergyPerkIds":["breakout","saboteur","background-player","were-gonna-live-forever"],"synergyOther":[],"antiSynergyPerkIds":[],"archetypeRatings":[],"reviewFlags":["v15-schema-migrated","queue-rating:audit-explicit"],"synergies":["Breakout","Saboteur","Background Player","We're Gonna Live Forever"],"antiSynergies":[],"name":"Mettle of Man","alternateName":null,"source":"Ash Williams","status":"Live 10.2.0","currentEffect":"After you trigger a third Protection Hit by any means, the perk activates. While Injured, it shields you from the next attack that would put you into the Dying State. After you heal to full health by any means, the Killer sees your Aura whenever you are farther than the tier-specific distance from them. The perk deactivates when you enter the Dying State by any means. It increases your chance to be the initial Obsession by +100%; a Killer can have only one Obsession at a time.","activation":["Trigger a third Protection Hit by any means.","Be Injured for the protective shield to apply.","Heal to full health for the Killer-aura reveal component to apply.","Ends/deactivates when: Deactivates when you enter the Dying State by any means.","Ends/deactivates when: The Killer-aura reveal applies only while you are farther than 12/14/16 metres from the Killer."],"patchNote":"Latest live balance change (6.2.0): Restored its pre-6.1.2 behavior and allowed it to activate and trigger more than once.","plainEnglishSummary":"After three Protection Hits, it can prevent one hit from downing you and later reveals your Aura to the Killer at long range.","cooldown":null,"duration":[],"tokenOrStackBehavior":"No visible token counter is specified. Each activation requires three Protection Hits; following deactivation, it can activate again after another three Protection Hits.","oncePerTrialOrOtherLimits":"Can activate more than once in a Trial after earning another three Protection Hits. The Killer can be Obsession with only one Survivor at a time.","statusEffectsInvolved":[],"specialInteractions":["The protective effect shields against the next attack that would put you into the Dying State; it is not the Endurance Status Effect."],"sourceCharacter":"Ash Williams","isGeneralPerk":false,"currentLivePatchVerified":"10.2.0"},{"id":"aftercare","rank":105,"tier":"B","roles":["Information","Team Support"],"summary":"Create mutual Aura links with Survivors you heal, unhook, or receive healing/unhooks from, up to three teammates; all links disappear when you are hooked.","metaStatus":"Good","skillLevel":"Low","soloQ":3,"swf":3,"unlockPriority":"Medium","glossaryKeys":["aura-reading","solo-q","hook-state"],"useCases":["Build near-global teammate information through normal altruistic interactions.","Maintain awareness of linked teammates without requiring proximity.","Coordinate rescues and healing in Solo Q through persistent Aura links."],"counters":["Being hooked erases every link.","You must interact with teammates before information exists.","Early-game value can be zero before links are established."],"pros":["Mutual information can cover multiple teammates.","Links can last a long time if you avoid hook.","Excellent information density once fully built."],"cons":["Hook reset is severe.","Needs setup interactions.","Bond offers simpler immediate information."],"analysis":["Aftercare takes this position because its fully built state is genuinely strong. Three mutual Aura links can create something close to permanent team awareness, letting linked Survivors find each other for heals, rescues, and rotations.","The setup is natural enough: heal someone, unhook them, or receive those actions. The issue is not building links once, but preserving them. A single hook on the perk owner wipes the entire network.","That reset makes the perk feast-or-famine. A Survivor who avoids hook for a long stretch can enjoy excellent information, while someone found early may spend most of the match rebuilding.","Aftercare is therefore a good but fragile Solo Q information perk. Bond is less ambitious but much more reliable, which explains the large ranking gap between them."],"verdict":"Excellent once established, painfully fragile once you are hooked. Aftercare can create a beautiful information network that the Killer resets with one successful chase.","publicationStatus":"published","tags":["Team","Aura Reading"],"queueRatingStatus":"reviewed","rankRange":null,"rankConfidence":"Not assessed","rankStatus":"inherited","evidenceStatus":"inherited","acquisition":{"type":"character","sourceCharacter":"Jeff Johansen"},"synergyPerkIds":["bond","kindred","well-make-it","empathic-connection"],"synergyOther":[],"antiSynergyPerkIds":[],"archetypeRatings":[],"reviewFlags":["v15-schema-migrated","queue-rating:normalized-tier-plus-v14-specialization-signal"],"synergies":["Bond","Kindred","We'll Make It","Empathic Connection"],"antiSynergies":[],"name":"Aftercare","alternateName":null,"source":"Jeff Johansen","status":"Live 10.2.0","currentEffect":"You see the Auras of up to 1/2/3 most recent Survivors who unhooked or healed you, or whom you unhooked or healed. Each linked Survivor also sees your Aura. All Aura links reset when the Killer hooks you.","activation":["You or another Survivor heals or unhooks the other.","Ends/deactivates when: All Aura links reset when the Killer hooks you."],"patchNote":"Latest live balance change (unknown): No material live balance change could be verified from available patch history.","plainEnglishSummary":"Healing and unhooking creates mutual Aura links with up to three of your most recent qualifying teammates; all links reset when you are hooked.","cooldown":null,"duration":["Aura links persist until the Killer hooks you."],"tokenOrStackBehavior":"Links update to the most recent qualifying Survivors, up to 1/2/3 by tier.","oncePerTrialOrOtherLimits":null,"statusEffectsInvolved":[],"specialInteractions":["Each link is mutual: both linked Survivors see the other's Aura."],"sourceCharacter":"Jeff Johansen","isGeneralPerk":false,"currentLivePatchVerified":"10.2.0"},{"id":"self-preservation","rank":106,"tier":"B","roles":["Stealth","Rescue"],"summary":"Whenever another Survivor is hooked, gain Elusive for up to 15 seconds, suppressing Aura, Scratch Marks, Blood, and pain sounds.","metaStatus":"Good","skillLevel":"Low–Medium","soloQ":3,"swf":3,"unlockPriority":"Medium","glossaryKeys":["hook-state","aura-reading"],"useCases":["Rotate safely after another Survivor is hooked while common post-hook information perks may be active.","Hide several tracking channels at once during a dangerous Killer rotation.","Continue a nearby objective with reduced risk of being immediately located."],"counters":["The perk only triggers when another Survivor is hooked.","Killer Instinct, direct sight, and other non-covered information can still reveal you.","If the Killer does not rotate toward you, much of the 13/14/15-second protection may be unnecessary.","Basekit post-unhook Elusive overlaps part of this perk's tracking-denial value during the first 10 seconds after rescue."],"pros":["Elusive suppresses multiple tracking channels simultaneously.","Automatic trigger with no execution requirement.","Current 9.5-era design is much broader than the perk's older form."],"cons":["Hook-dependent and reactive.","Does not help when you are the Survivor being hooked.","Protection may be wasted if the Killer remains near the hook or chases someone else."],"analysis":["Self-Preservation kept the same broad Elusive package in 10.2 but lost half of its old Tier III duration, falling from thirty seconds to fifteen.","Fifteen seconds is still enough to hide a post-hook rotation or remain on a nearby objective through common Aura-reading windows. The effect continues to suppress several tracking channels at once rather than one specific cue.","The shorter window makes wasted triggers more painful. If the Killer stays on the hooked Survivor or rotates elsewhere, the protection can expire before it is tested.","The perk remains useful, especially in Solo Q, but its old ranking should come down because the duration nerf directly attacks its consistency."],"verdict":"Same strong Elusive package, much shorter clock. Self-Preservation is still useful after teammate hooks, but 15 seconds demands better timing than the old 30.","publicationStatus":"published","reviewFlags":["10.2-live-change","v15-schema-migrated","queue-rating:normalized-tier-plus-v14-specialization-signal"],"tags":["Information Denial","Hook"],"queueRatingStatus":"reviewed","rankRange":null,"rankConfidence":"Not assessed","rankStatus":"inherited","evidenceStatus":"inherited","acquisition":{"type":"character","sourceCharacter":"Lee Yun-Jin"},"synergyPerkIds":["distortion","iron-will","lightweight","deja-vu"],"synergyOther":[],"antiSynergyPerkIds":[],"archetypeRatings":[],"synergies":["Distortion","Iron Will","Lightweight","Déjà Vu"],"antiSynergies":[],"name":"Self-Preservation","alternateName":null,"source":"Lee Yun-Jin","status":"Live 10.2.0","currentEffect":"Whenever another Survivor is hooked, you gain Elusive for 13/14/15 seconds. Elusive suppresses your Aura, Scratch Marks, Pools of Blood, and Grunts of Pain.","activation":["Another Survivor is hooked.","Ends/deactivates when: Elusive expires after 13/14/15 seconds; Elusive may also end early under its status-effect rules."],"patchNote":"Latest live balance change (10.2.0): Reduced Elusive duration after another Survivor is hooked from 20/25/30 to 13/14/15 seconds.","plainEnglishSummary":"When another Survivor is hooked, briefly hides your Aura and tracking traces from the Killer.","cooldown":null,"duration":["Elusive: 13/14/15 seconds."],"tokenOrStackBehavior":null,"oncePerTrialOrOtherLimits":null,"statusEffectsInvolved":["Elusive"],"specialInteractions":["Elusive hides the Survivor's Aura and suppresses Scratch Marks, Pools of Blood, and Grunts of Pain."],"sourceCharacter":"Lee Yun-Jin","isGeneralPerk":false,"currentLivePatchVerified":"10.2.0"},{"id":"bite-the-bullet","rank":107,"tier":"B","roles":["Healing","Stealth","Skill Check"],"summary":"While healing yourself or someone else, suppress healing sounds and your Grunts of Pain; failed healing Skill Checks no longer alert the Killer and lose very little progress.","metaStatus":"Good","skillLevel":"Low–Medium","soloQ":4,"swf":3,"unlockPriority":"Medium","glossaryKeys":["reset","health-state"],"useCases":["Hide a heal behind nearby cover while the Killer searches using sound.","Pair with Self-Care or other independent healing to create silent resets.","Reduce the punishment from missed healing Skill Checks."],"counters":["A Killer with direct vision or Aura reading can still find the heal.","Silent healing does not make the interaction faster.","Strong players rarely plan around missed Skill Checks."],"pros":["Completely removes important healing audio cues.","Works on self-heals and teammate heals.","Failed Skill Checks become much safer."],"cons":["No speed bonus.","Requires a situation where sound actually matters.","Can encourage slow hidden healing instead of productive objective play."],"analysis":["Bite the Bullet closes the top one hundred because silent healing can create clever escapes and resets, but it solves a narrower problem than the perks above it. Removing healing sounds and Grunts of Pain can make nearby searches surprisingly difficult when line of sight is already broken.","The perk pairs naturally with Self-Care and tracking-denial builds. A Killer may follow a trail into an area and expect to hear an injured Survivor healing, only to receive no useful sound cue.","The Skill Check protection is mostly insurance. Experienced players should not miss many standard healing checks, so the reduced progress loss and lack of a Loud Noise notification are helpful but not central to the ranking.","Bite the Bullet remains B because stealth healing can also become a tempo trap. Spending a long time hiding and healing silently is not automatically good play. The perk is best when silence changes a real Killer search, not when it merely makes a slow heal quieter."],"verdict":"A clever stealth-healing tool that can hide a reset under the Killer's nose. Bite the Bullet is useful, but silence alone does not make an inefficient heal efficient.","publicationStatus":"published","tags":[],"queueRatingStatus":"reviewed","rankRange":null,"rankConfidence":"Not assessed","rankStatus":"inherited","evidenceStatus":"inherited","acquisition":{"type":"character","sourceCharacter":"Leon S. Kennedy"},"synergyPerkIds":["self-care","lucky-break","iron-will","botany-knowledge"],"synergyOther":[],"antiSynergyPerkIds":[],"archetypeRatings":[],"reviewFlags":["v15-schema-migrated","queue-rating:normalized-tier-plus-v14-specialization-signal"],"synergies":["Self-Care","Lucky Break","Iron Will","Botany Knowledge"],"antiSynergies":[],"name":"Bite the Bullet","alternateName":null,"source":"Leon S. Kennedy","status":"Live 10.2.0","currentEffect":"While healing yourself or another Survivor, suppress your Grunts of Pain and the sounds of the Healing action. Missing a Healing Skill Check creates no Loud Noise notification; instead it loses an additional 3/2/1% of total Healing progress.","activation":["Begin a Healing action on yourself or another Survivor.","Ends/deactivates when: Sound suppression ends when the Healing action ends."],"patchNote":"Latest live balance change (unknown): No material live balance change could be verified from available patch history.","plainEnglishSummary":"Healing becomes silent, and a missed Healing Skill Check costs extra progress instead of notifying the Killer.","cooldown":null,"duration":["While healing."],"tokenOrStackBehavior":null,"oncePerTrialOrOtherLimits":null,"statusEffectsInvolved":[],"specialInteractions":["A missed Healing Skill Check has no Loud Noise notification; extra progress loss depends on tier."],"sourceCharacter":"Leon S. Kennedy","isGeneralPerk":false,"currentLivePatchVerified":"10.2.0"},{"id":"blood-pact","rank":108,"tier":"B","roles":["Mobility","Healing","Utility"],"summary":"While you are not the Obsession, you and the injured Obsession see each other; after either heals the other, both gain up to 7% Haste while staying within 16 metres.","metaStatus":"Good","skillLevel":"Medium–High","soloQ":2,"swf":4,"unlockPriority":"Medium","glossaryKeys":["haste","aura-reading","swf"],"useCases":["Create a powerful two-person Haste pair after a heal.","Use mutual Aura information to locate the Obsession when either of you is injured.","Coordinate paired rotations or loops where both Survivors can remain within the Haste radius.","If you are the Obsession and get hooked, the Obsession can transfer to another Survivor, allowing the perk to become usable again afterward."],"counters":["The perk is disabled while you are the Obsession.","The Haste disappears when the pair separates beyond the allowed range.","Staying close together can create inefficient map pressure or expose two Survivors to the Killer."],"pros":["Seven percent Haste is a major movement bonus.","Mutual Aura information helps the pair reunite.","No fixed duration while the proximity condition is maintained."],"cons":["Obsession restriction can disable the perk completely.","Tether requirement is awkward.","Grouping two Survivors can be strategically dangerous."],"analysis":["Blood Pact ranks here because 7% Haste is too large to dismiss, even with a frustrating tether condition. After the relevant heal, two Survivors can move significantly faster for as long as they remain within sixteen metres of each other.","The mutual Aura reading helps create the setup. When either you or the Obsession is injured, finding the other player is easy, making the heal trigger more practical than a blind teammate search.","The problem is what happens afterward. Dead by Daylight usually rewards Survivors for spreading pressure, while Blood Pact wants two people to stay close. In chase that can create bodyblocks and unusual movement advantages, but on generators it can encourage inefficient grouping.","The perk also shuts off entirely if you are the Obsession, though it reduces the chance of starting that way. Blood Pact has an excellent ceiling in a coordinated pair and enough awkward conditions to remain B."],"verdict":"Seven percent Haste can be outrageous, but Blood Pact asks two Survivors to stay tethered together and can disable itself through the Obsession system. Strong in a plan, awkward in ordinary play.","publicationStatus":"published","reviewFlags":["10.2-live-change","v15-schema-migrated","queue-rating:normalized-tier-plus-v14-specialization-signal"],"tags":["Haste","Obsession"],"queueRatingStatus":"reviewed","rankRange":null,"rankConfidence":"Not assessed","rankStatus":"inherited","evidenceStatus":"inherited","acquisition":{"type":"character","sourceCharacter":"Cheryl Mason"},"synergyPerkIds":["teamwork-power-of-two","a-place-for-us","botany-knowledge","hope"],"synergyOther":[],"antiSynergyPerkIds":[],"archetypeRatings":[],"synergies":["Teamwork: Power of Two","A Place for Us","Botany Knowledge","Hope"],"antiSynergies":[],"name":"Blood Pact","alternateName":null,"source":"Cheryl Mason","status":"Live 10.2.0","currentEffect":"While you are not the Obsession, if you or the Obsession is injured, you see each other's Auras. When you finish healing the Obsession or they finish healing you, both gain 5/6/7% Haste while within 16 metres of each other; this lasts as long as you remain within that range. While you are the Obsession, if you are hooked, another Survivor becomes the Obsession. At Trial start, you are less likely to become the Obsession.","activation":["You are not the Obsession for the mutual Aura and post-heal Haste effects.","You or the Obsession is injured for the Aura link.","Complete a qualifying heal while within 16 metres for Haste.","If you are the Obsession, being hooked transfers the Obsession to another Survivor.","Ends/deactivates when: The Aura link ends when neither you nor the Obsession is injured, or while you are the Obsession.","Ends/deactivates when: The post-heal Haste ends when you and the Obsession are no longer within 16 metres of each other; it has no fixed time limit."],"patchNote":"Latest live balance change (10.2.0): Added an Obsession-transfer effect: if you are the Obsession and are hooked, another Survivor becomes the Obsession; existing Aura, Haste, and initial-Obsession modifiers remain.","plainEnglishSummary":"While you are not the Obsession, you share injury-based Aura information and can gain shared Haste after healing each other; if you are the Obsession and get hooked, the Obsession transfers.","cooldown":null,"duration":["Post-heal Haste lasts for as long as both Survivors remain within 16 metres of each other; no fixed duration."],"tokenOrStackBehavior":null,"oncePerTrialOrOtherLimits":null,"statusEffectsInvolved":["Haste"],"specialInteractions":["At Trial start, you are less likely to be selected as the Obsession.","If you are the Obsession and are hooked, another Survivor becomes the Obsession."],"sourceCharacter":"Cheryl Mason","isGeneralPerk":false,"currentLivePatchVerified":"10.2.0"}]);
